.md as reference.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ56GN85EQE03SZAEPK19DNQ\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T12:10:19.269Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Wrote templates/skills/review/SKILL.md (168 lines). NEW skill — extracted kspec-specific review concerns into a generic building block. Covers: spec alignment verification, own AC coverage (annotation format, checking), trait AC coverage (inherited ACs, N/A handling), validation integration (exit codes, error vs warning), review checklist (MUST-FIX/SHOULD-FIX/SUGGESTION), severity guide, guidance for wrapping in project-specific reviews. Not a full local-review replacement — no project-specific test commands. Added manifest entry. All 3181 tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHZHPT0KJ5QKX8A9S9YE8Y57\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Purge project-specific skill references from shared templates and docs\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Remove references to /pr, /pr-review, /local-review, /release from templates/agents-sections/ and any generated docs or code that ships with kspec. These are project-specific skills that should not be in shared/core content. Audit: (1) templates/agents-sections/*.md for skill references, (2) src/ for hardcoded skill names in strings or help text, (3) kspec-agents.md generation code for skill assumptions. Replace with /kspec:review where appropriate for review-related references. Ensure the purge does not break this project — the project-specific skills still exist in .claude/skills/, they just should not be referenced by shipped code.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #463. Purged all project-specific skill references (/pr, /pr-review, /local-review, /release, /triage, /reflect, /task-work) from shipped templates and source code. Templates use generic language or kspec: namespace skills. Ralph prompt builders now receive skill names from config (ralph.skills section in kspec.config.yaml) with kspec: namespace defaults. Fix cycle addressed initial review finding that constants still shipped project-specific names. All 3177 tests pass, CI green.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@01KHZHPG\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"core-skills\",\n      \"cleanup\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-21T07:30:28.499Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T09:41:59.151Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T09:52:43.257Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V5DVM4SAQNNZQ6CXX8FFP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:51:56.916Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Standalone cleanup. Audit templates/agents-sections/*.md for /pr, /pr-review, /local-review, /release refs. Replace with /kspec:review where appropriate.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4WCSFEX47F26NEQKBE5FDH\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T09:13:26.767Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Audited templates/agents-sections/ and src/ for project-specific skill references. Changes: (1) 04-pr-workflow.md: replaced /local-review, /pr, /pr-review with generic workflow-based language. (2) 03-task-lifecycle.md: /triage → /kspec:triage (core skill), /reflect → generic 'during reflection'. (3) src/ralph/subagent.ts: extracted SKILL_PR_REVIEW, SKILL_REFLECT, SKILL_TASK_WORK constants — skill invocations now use constants instead of hardcoded strings. (4) src/cli/commands/ralph.ts: updated to use constants. (5) Regenerated kspec-agents.md. (6) Updated tests to use constants. All 3173 tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4X9H26V9F6YJYX11BAE4GP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T09:29:08.422Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX confirmed: src/ralph/subagent.ts still ships project-specific skill names (/pr-review, /task-work, /reflect) in constants that get embedded in ralph prompts. Task requires purging these from shipped code. Either use core kspec: namespace skills or pull skill names from project meta config. Templates were cleaned correctly.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4Y0RJRKX4Z5TJ0HHRTM17E\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T09:41:49.784Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Fixed: Replaced project-specific skill names (/task-work, /reflect, /pr-review) with kspec: namespace defaults (/kspec:task-work, /kspec:reflect, /kspec:review). Added ralph.skills config section to kspec.config.yaml for project-level overrides. Threaded config through prompt builders. All 3177 tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHZHZ7GGQ6710KHVNVJB3GEB\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Fix task get to display description field in text output\",\n    \"type\": \"bug\",\n    \"description\": \"Bug: `kspec task get` omits the task description field from output. Shows title, status, spec context, and notes — but not the description. Critical for triage and automation where descriptions carry context that specs/notes do not.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #439. Added task description display in formatTaskDetails() with whitespace-only guard. Two new AC-annotated tests.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"cli\",\n      \"bug\",\n      \"dx\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-21T07:35:04.464Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-21T07:35:09.785Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-21T14:43:55.118Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KHZJ60P7SWM2JR6XDDWMCPWP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-21T07:38:46.855Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Fixed: added task.description display in formatTaskDetails() in output.ts. Shows as a Description section between automation and spec_ref fields. Added 2 test cases verifying text output includes/excludes description appropriately.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHZMQ8YTV97DQ12GGR7SGJQX\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"ws\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Whitespace existing\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"valid\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"cancelled\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Test task artifact — no real work\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-21T08:23:09.530Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ19D0CH3SECG4FT9GQ46S10\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-plugin-rendering\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Migrate skill rendering to Claude Code plugin system\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Claude Code does not support nested skill directories (.claude/skills/kspec/<id>/ is NOT discovered). The official namespacing mechanism is the plugin system.\\n\\n## Goal\\n\\nRender kspec core skills as a Claude Code plugin so they are properly namespaced and discovered. For non-Claude platforms (Codex, etc.), use flat prefix naming since they lack plugins.\\n\\n### Claude Code target structure\\n.claude/plugins/kspec/.claude-plugin/plugin.json (name, version, description)\\n.claude/plugins/kspec/skills/help/SKILL.md -> invoked as /kspec:help\\n\\n### Non-Claude target structure\\n.agents/skills/kspec-help/SKILL.md (flat prefix)\\n\\n## Key Implementation Points\\n\\n### Path construction (3 strategic functions in skill-render.ts)\\n- getSkillSubdir() - currently adds kspec/ prefix for core skills on claude-code\\n- getRenderedSkillPath() - constructs full output path\\n- getPlatformDefaultOutputDir() - returns .claude/skills for claude-code\\n- claudeCodeRenderer defaultOutputDir needs to change for core skills\\n\\n### Plugin manifest generation\\n- Generate .claude/plugins/kspec/.claude-plugin/plugin.json during skill render\\n- Include kspec version, description\\n\\n### Migration\\n- Remove old .claude/skills/kspec/ directory (monolithic skill + broken nested renders)\\n- skill render --clean needs to handle old to new path transition\\n- Similar pattern to PR #440 migration logic\\n\\n### Non-Claude platforms\\n- Codex renderer uses .agents/skills/ (flat) - use kspec-<id> prefix instead of nesting\\n- Other future platforms: same flat prefix approach\\n\\n### Files affected (from codebase exploration)\\n- src/parser/skill-render.ts - core path logic, PlatformRenderer, claudeCodeRenderer\\n- src/cli/commands/skill-diff.ts - render/status/diff/verify commands\\n- src/cli/commands/setup.ts - getSetupStatus() directory scanning\\n- src/parser/validate-skills.ts - findSkillFiles() directory discovery\\n- 14 test suites with path assertions\\n\\n### What already exists\\n- templates/skills/help/SKILL.md - lean CLI map content ready for plugin rendering\\n- templates/skills/manifest.yaml - core skills manifest\\n- PlatformRenderer interface is well-abstracted\\n\\n### Also resolve\\n- Existing monolithic .claude/skills/kspec/SKILL.md (591 lines) replaced by plugin-rendered skills\\n- kspec-agents.md Finding Information table should show /kspec:help after migration (fix generateSkillsTable in agent-data-sections.ts)\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #442. Core skills now render to .claude/plugins/kspec/skills/<id>/ for proper Claude Code plugin discovery as /kspec:<id>.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"core-skills\",\n      \"plugins\",\n      \"platform\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-21T23:43:47.601Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-21T23:56:39.092Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-22T01:37:33.612Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ1A326HT5QZJ9AVXTGRDH21\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-21T23:55:50.353Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"NOTE: PR #440 namespace rendering (.claude/skills/kspec/<id>/) is also broken — Claude Code does not discover nested skill dirs. Plugin migration must clean up the merged PR #440 output structure too, not just the attempted help skill rename.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ1C8WW2YPZGCTMFE3ZKVDMD\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T00:33:58.658Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation complete. All code changes done and verified:\\n\\n1. **skill-render.ts**: Added PLUGIN_DIR/PLUGIN_SKILLS_DIR constants. getSkillSubdir() returns just skillId for core+claude-code (plugin provides namespace), kspec-<id> for core+codex. getRenderedSkillPath() routes core→plugin dir. claudeCodeRenderer renders core to plugin dir, cleans 3 old path formats, generates plugin manifest. codexRenderer uses kspec-<id> subdir. Both drift checkers updated.\\n\\n2. **agent-data-sections.ts**: Core skills invoked as /kspec:<id>, project as /<id>.\\n\\n3. **validate-skills.ts**: Scans .claude/plugins/*/skills/ for SKILL.md files.\\n\\n4. **setup-status.ts & setup.ts**: Both scan plugin dirs for skill counts.\\n\\n5. **skill-diff.ts**: Status/diff/clean all use correct paths. Clean scans plugin dir + migrates old .claude/skills/kspec/ remnants.\\n\\n6. **Tests**: core-skill-namespace (15 tests), supporting-files-convention (12), agent-data-sections (28) — all pass. 159 related tests pass total.\\n\\n7. **Spec**: @skill-rendering ac-7 updated to reference plugin path.\\n\\n8. **Verified**: kspec skill render/status/clean/validate all work correctly. kspec-agents.md shows /kspec:kspec-help.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ315WHBK8887TZQXY8HG9DH\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Spike: Design interactive triage system with persistent metadata\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Spike complete. Plan imported with 6 specs and 6 tasks. Dependencies set.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"spike\",\n      \"design\",\n      \"inbox\",\n      \"triage\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T15:58:34.538Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-22T20:16:48.921Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-22T20:16:53.170Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3168YTVCBZ7EPD5W213YPA\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T15:58:47.258Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Spike to explore design space and produce spec-plan for interactive triage system.\\n\\n## Problem\\nInbox triage is currently agent-driven and ephemeral. Triage decisions (reasoning, evidence, actions, user decisions) are lost between sessions. No way for users to interactively review/override agent triage. No way for subsequent agents to act on prior triage work reliably.\\n\\n## Design Space\\n\\n### 1. Triage Metadata on Inbox Items\\nAdd structured fields: triage_status, triage_reasoning, triage_evidence, triage_action, user_decision, spec_gap flag, automation_eligible flag. Key question: extend InboxItem schema or separate TriageRecord?\\n\\n### 2. Interactive Triage UI (Web UI via Daemon)\\nPer-category triage mode with one-by-one item presentation. Shows description, agent reasoning, evidence, recommended action. User chooses from options or overrides. Free-form input for reasoning. Next/previous navigation. Writes through daemon API to shadow branch.\\n\\n### 3. Agent Handoff Export\\nContext-rich export of triage decisions for fresh agent sessions. Include full item context, triage metadata, user decision, relevant refs. Format must give new agents enough context to act without re-researching. Possibly: kspec inbox export --triaged\\n\\n### 4. Daemon API Extensions\\nGET/PUT /api/inbox/:ref/triage, filtering by triage_status, bulk updates.\\n\\n## Key Questions\\n- Schema: inline on inbox items or separate triage records?\\n- History: version triage decisions (agent triages, user overrides)?\\n- Workflow: integrate with existing /triage skill?\\n- Export: what format maximizes agent effectiveness?\\n\\n## References\\n- Triage skill: .claude/skills/triage/\\n- Inbox schema: src/schema/inbox.ts  \\n- Daemon API: packages/daemon/src/\\n- Web UI inbox: packages/web-ui/src/routes/inbox/\\n- Triage report artifact: .kspec/artifacts/triage-report-2026-02-22.html (example of current ephemeral output)\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ316F9ESM6V9JBSKEYDA163\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Spec and formalize .kspec/artifacts/ directory convention\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@artifacts-directory\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #446. Artifacts directory convention implemented: init/setup/repair create .kspec/artifacts/, doctor health check, .gitignore exclusion, 6 tests. Codex review noted: spec wording re .gitkeep should be updated (intentionally skipped since dir is gitignored), setup hardcodes .kspec path (low-risk), repair doesn't ensure .gitignore for legacy branches.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"spec\",\n      \"dx\",\n      \"convention\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T15:58:53.742Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-22T17:47:04.173Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-22T18:30:32.817Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ316VA1XV93XEQH15S54FN5\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T15:59:06.049Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Directory created and gitignored. Remaining work is spec + documentation.\\n\\n## Done\\n- Created .kspec/artifacts/ directory\\n- Added .kspec/.gitignore to exclude artifacts/ from shadow branch commits\\n- Moved first artifact (triage-report-2026-02-22.html) there\\n\\n## Remaining (needs spec)\\n- Spec the convention: what goes in artifacts, naming patterns, lifecycle\\n- Add to kspec setup: create artifacts/ dir during init\\n- Document in AGENTS.md or template sections: when to use artifacts/ vs other locations\\n- Consider: kspec artifacts list, kspec artifacts clean --older-than Nd\\n- Consider: should agents auto-name artifacts with date prefix? (current: triage-report-2026-02-22.html)\\n- Add to doctor command: check artifacts/ exists\\n\\n## Design Questions\\n- Should artifacts be purely ephemeral or optionally tracked?\\n- Naming convention: <type>-<date>.ext? <type>-<session-id>.ext?\\n- Max size/age policy?\\n- Should kspec generate commands output to artifacts/ by default?\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ37C8HXX2K25VFZNCKSBWJN\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T17:46:54.909Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Spec created: @artifacts-directory with 8 ACs covering init, setup, doctor, repair, gitignore, naming convention, and empty dir persistence. Review identified key gaps: .gitkeep for empty dir survival, name collision handling, shadow repair behavior, and AC redundancy — all addressed in final spec. Implementation scope: modify init (shadow.ts), setup pipeline, doctor checks, and shadow repair to create/check .kspec/artifacts/ with .gitkeep.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ37TGWDEGXT1KHDRJNNYQVV\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T17:54:42.189Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation complete for 6 of 8 ACs:\\n\\n- ac-init-creates: initializeShadow() creates artifacts/ dir (shadow.ts ~line 1708)\\n- ac-gitignore-entry: .gitignore with artifacts/ written during init (shadow.ts ~line 1710)\\n- ac-commits-exclude: Covered by gitignore — tested that git add -A doesn't stage artifacts\\n- ac-setup-ensures: runSetupPipeline() creates artifacts/ if missing (setup.ts ~line 1542)\\n- ac-doctor-checks: buildShadowSection() checks artifactsDirExists (doctor.ts ~line 257)\\n- ac-repair-recreates: repairShadow() creates artifacts/ after worktree rebuild (shadow.ts ~line 1818)\\n\\nConvention-only ACs (no code enforcement):\\n- ac-naming-convention: Documented pattern type-YYYY-MM-DD.ext — agents follow by reading spec\\n- ac-empty-dir-persistence: Handled by init/setup/repair creating the dir (not via .gitkeep since gitignore excludes artifacts/)\\n\\nTests added: 6 new tests across shadow.test.ts and doctor.test.ts. All 112+29 pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ32FKT1753QRTAPVDGG1KHB\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Fix plugin marketplace: add marketplace.json and validate directory source setup\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #445. Generated marketplace.json for directory source, restructured plugin to plugins/kspec/ matching official pattern, fixed MarketplaceEntry type, added ac-6 test coverage, updated spec ac-5 path.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"plugin\",\n      \"bug\",\n      \"cli\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T16:21:21.857Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-22T16:44:02.493Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-22T17:34:56.312Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ32G0SA5R029XAKHQSBN9V2\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T16:21:35.146Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Spec gap: plugin marketplace registration is incomplete.\\n\\n## Problem\\nkspec setup registers a 'directory' source marketplace but the plugin/ dir only has .claude-plugin/plugin.json (single plugin manifest). Claude Code expects .claude-plugin/marketplace.json (marketplace listing format) for directory sources. Warning: 'Failed to load marketplace kspec-plugins: marketplace.json not found'.\\n\\n## What Exists\\n- plugin/.claude-plugin/plugin.json - single plugin manifest (name, version, description)\\n- plugin/skills/help/SKILL.md - one core skill\\n- src/lib/claude-plugin-registry.ts - registers marketplace in known_marketplaces.json\\n- Build step populates plugin/ from templates/skills/\\n\\n## What's Missing\\n1. marketplace.json generation: build step should produce .claude-plugin/marketplace.json wrapping the kspec plugin entry in the marketplace plugins array format\\n2. Validate against official marketplace schema (see ~/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/claude-plugins-official/.claude-plugin/marketplace.json for reference format)\\n3. Spec coverage: review @plugin-rendering and @core-skill-installation specs for marketplace.json AC gaps\\n4. Test: verify claude doctor shows no plugin errors after setup\\n\\n## Reference\\n- Fix commit: 47453817 (directory source type fix)\\n- Official marketplace format: { name, description, owner, plugins: [{ name, description, version, source, ... }] }\\n- PR #444 shipped the plugin system but missed marketplace.json requirement\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ34AP3V2JACQ9Z0NHS7FSFK\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T16:53:37.531Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Added marketplace.json generation to build-plugin.cjs. Fixed MarketplaceEntry type (source was string, now object). Updated test assertion from 'local' to directory source object. Added ac-6 to @package-distribution for marketplace.json coverage. Pre-existing failures: daemon-executable compilation and doctor daemon checks (unrelated).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ355AM9WTD3DGBE63J50ZQV\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T17:08:10.505Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Verified: Claude Code no longer shows marketplace warning. marketplace.json generated with ./plugins/kspec source path matching official marketplace pattern. Plugin loads successfully.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ355T6TYSYQMMX6H7RJVWSC\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T17:08:26.458Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Leaving in_progress pending user decision: fold test quality improvement (structural validation vs exact output matching) into this task or capture separately.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3FXH3T2RJQSNZAMPPF12ES\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"implement-interactive-triage-system\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement Interactive Triage System\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@interactive-triage\",\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@plan-interactive-triage-system\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #450. Parent spec @interactive-triage ac-1 and ac-2 proven with integration tests: end-to-end decision chain test (agent record → override → act → export with attribution/timestamp verification in export output) and persistence test (records survive inbox deletion). Codex review caught incomplete ac-2 coverage in export assertions — fixed in follow-up commit. All CI green.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T20:16:09.338Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-22T23:46:26.320Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T00:07:58.393Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3FXH3T3TDK0K5CAHT2EMCN\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T20:16:09.338Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"See plan @plan-interactive-triage-system for implementation notes\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3W27E6CSAET35XKYFTRV2Y\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T23:48:26.182Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Parent spec @interactive-triage has 2 high-level ACs that were already fully satisfied by child implementations (triage record schema + CLI commands). Added AC annotations to existing tests and 2 new integration tests: (1) end-to-end decision chain test exercising agent record → user override → act → export with full attribution verification, (2) record persistence test verifying triage records survive inbox item deletion. All 72 triage tests passing.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3FXHDH6X85QF35D56P2F69\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"implement-triage-record-schema\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement Triage Record Schema\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@triage-record-schema\",\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@plan-interactive-triage-system\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Schema and parser implemented with full AC coverage (38 tests). Committed in aac8bc27.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T20:16:09.649Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-22T20:16:58.536Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-22T20:23:31.838Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3FXHDHXHD05K28G8JQXVWX\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T20:16:09.649Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation notes:\\n\\nCreate src/schema/triage.ts following plan.ts pattern.\\nTriageStatusSchema = z.enum([\\\"pending\\\", \\\"triaged\\\", \\\"acted_on\\\"]).\\nTriageActionSchema = z.enum([\\\"promote\\\", \\\"delete\\\", \\\"defer\\\", \\\"spec-gap\\\", \\\"duplicate\\\"]).\\nInclude updated_at field set on any mutation.\\nEnforce inbox_ref uniqueness in save logic (upsert pattern).\\nAdd load/save in src/parser/yaml.ts: getTriageFilePath, loadTriageRecords, saveTriageRecord.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3GA0ENHKF8G4J83AFESZ0V\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T20:22:58.261Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented schema and parser layer:\\n\\n**Schema (src/schema/triage.ts):**\\n- TriageStatusSchema: pending | triaged | acted_on\\n- TriageActionSchema: promote | delete | defer | spec-gap | duplicate\\n- TriageRecordSchema: full record with decision, override, and execution fields\\n- TriageRecordInputSchema: input variant for creation\\n- TriageFileSchema: collection format with kynetic_triage version string\\n\\n**Parser (src/parser/yaml.ts):**\\n- getTriageFilePath(ctx) — returns project.triage.yaml path\\n- loadTriageRecords(ctx) — loads and validates triage records\\n- saveTriageRecord(ctx, record) — upsert by ULID or inbox_ref, sets updated_at\\n- findTriageRecordByRef(records, ref) — lookup by ULID/short ULID\\n- findTriageRecordByInboxRef(records, inboxRef) — lookup by inbox item reference\\n\\n**Tests (38 passing):**\\n- tests/triage-schema.test.ts — 21 tests covering all 9 ACs\\n- tests/triage-parser.test.ts — 17 tests covering load/save/find operations\\n\\nAll ACs covered. Full test suite green (3 pre-existing failures unrelated).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3FXHPC8CMZQFCC7SYGGMF8\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"implement-triage-cli-commands\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement Triage CLI Commands\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@triage-cli-commands\",\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@plan-interactive-triage-system\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #449. Implements all 7 triage CLI commands (record, list, act, override, export, start, get) with full own AC coverage (17/17) and comprehensive trait AC coverage across 6 traits (json-output, error-guidance, semantic-exit-codes, filterable-list, shadow-commit, dry-run). 52 tests passing. Fix cycle 2 resolved all previous review findings.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@implement-triage-record-schema\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T20:16:09.932Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-22T23:12:27.340Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-22T23:44:27.411Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3FXHPCXKGS393YJ3YK4TDW\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T20:16:09.932Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation notes:\\n\\nCreate src/cli/commands/triage.ts following inbox.ts pattern.\\nRegister via registerTriageCommands(program).\\nThe act command dispatches on record.action: promote reuses inbox\\npromote logic, delete reuses inbox delete logic, spec-gap creates\\nobservation, duplicate deletes inbox item, defer is a no-op transition.\\nInteractive start mode uses readline prompts.\\nOverride subcommand updates existing record with override fields.\\nExport subcommand delegates to shared formatter.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3S4ERBA3AJ4APZFKPFBYG2\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T22:57:13.483Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented all triage CLI commands:\\n\\n**Commands created (src/cli/commands/triage.ts):**\\n- `triage record <inbox-ref>` — Record a triage decision (ac-1, ac-11)\\n- `triage list` — List triage records with filters (ac-2, ac-3)\\n- `triage act <triage-ref>` — Execute triage decision (ac-4 through ac-8, ac-15, ac-16, ac-17)\\n- `triage override <triage-ref>` — Override existing decision (ac-12)\\n- `triage export` — Export as context markdown or JSON (ac-13, ac-14)\\n- `triage start` — Interactive triage mode (ac-9, ac-10)\\n- `triage get <triage-ref>` — Show record details\\n\\n**Action execution dispatch:**\\n- promote: Creates task from item_snapshot\\n- delete/duplicate: Deletes inbox item (prior authorization)\\n- defer: No-op transition\\n- spec-gap: Creates observation with item text + reasoning\\n\\n**Interactive mode:** Uses line-buffered readline for reliable piped stdin. Single rl interface for entire session.\\n\\n**Tests (35 passing):** All 17 ACs covered + trait ACs (json-output, error-guidance, filterable-list, shadow-commit, dry-run, semantic-exit-codes)\\n\\nFull test suite green (2 pre-existing failures unrelated).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3SAWV6HBKQ4V45E804F78P\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T23:00:44.519Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: Reverted submit - task is being handled by ralph loop, not this session\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3V419NGM1YF6RF3XADCBBC\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T23:31:56.853Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Addressed all 5 PR review findings:\\n\\nMUST-FIX resolved:\\n1. spec-gap observation: type changed to 'question', content prefixed with [spec-gap] marker. Verified with new test assertion checking observation type and content.\\n2. export --json precedence: Wrapped export output in output() function so globalOutputFormat (--json) takes precedence over --format option.\\n3. Trait AC coverage: Added 17 new tests covering @trait-filterable-list (ac-3,5,6), @trait-dry-run (ac-2,3,5), @trait-semantic-exit-codes (ac-1,2,5), @trait-error-guidance (ac-2,4,5,6), @trait-shadow-commit (ac-5). Updated annotations on existing tests.\\n\\nSHOULD-FIX resolved:\\n4. ac-10 test annotation clarified as partial (EOF preservation, not SIGINT).\\n5. triage list summary now uses post-filter count for accurate 'X of Y' display.\\n\\n52 tests passing. Full suite green (2 pre-existing failures unrelated).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3FXJ0DMK8EV8MW00D5PPCS\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"implement-triage-daemon-api\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement Triage Daemon API\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@triage-daemon-api\",\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@plan-interactive-triage-system\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #453. Implemented 6 triage API endpoints (GET list, GET export, POST create, GET single, POST override, POST act) with full own AC coverage (9/9), trait AC coverage (api-endpoint 5/6, websocket-protocol 1/1 route-level), 26 tests passing. Fix commit addressed upsert identity and stale metadata issues from initial review.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@implement-triage-record-schema\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T20:16:10.253Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T00:32:22.705Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T01:05:05.388Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3FXJ0D5HEVXGB714CPV356\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T20:16:10.253Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation notes:\\n\\nCreate packages/daemon/src/routes/triage.ts.\\nElysia prefix /api/triage with pubsub injection.\\nTopic triage:updates, events: triage_created, triage_updated, triage_acted.\\nRegister in server.ts alongside existing routes.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3Z6X22H1TRJQ32PDNV2AY9\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T00:43:25.122Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented triage daemon API routes at packages/daemon/src/routes/triage.ts. 6 endpoints: GET / (list), GET /export, POST / (create), GET /:ref, POST /:ref/override, POST /:ref/act. All 9 own ACs covered. Trait ACs: api-endpoint ac-1-5, websocket-protocol ac-3. Reused executeTriageAction from CLI. 24 tests passing.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3FXJ8ZEN8DSP3BD3HKP1SW\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"implement-interactive-triage-ui\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement Interactive Triage UI\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@interactive-triage-ui\",\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@plan-interactive-triage-system\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #455. Implemented interactive triage UI at /triage with card-based one-at-a-time presentation, action selection (5 actions), reasoning input, next/prev navigation with keyboard arrows, tag/status filters with progress bar, WebSocket triage:updates subscription for real-time updates, and static mode read-only support. All 8 own ACs and relevant trait ACs (ac-1-3) covered with 18 tests.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@implement-triage-daemon-api\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T20:16:10.527Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T01:38:03.792Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T02:07:33.821Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3FXJ90D9N8XRR2X7XWA8YF\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T20:16:10.528Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation notes:\\n\\nCreate packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte.\\nCard nav with index tracking. Progress bar (triaged/total).\\nAction buttons as button row. Textarea for reasoning.\\nSubscribe to triage:updates WebSocket topic.\\nAdd fetchTriage, createTriageRecord, updateTriageRecord to api.ts.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ432P0000E3EPD0N8EEG508\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T01:51:01.120Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented interactive triage UI at packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte. Card-based one-at-a-time presentation with: action selection (5 actions), reasoning textarea, next/prev navigation (keyboard arrows), tag/status filters with progress bar, WebSocket triage:updates subscription for real-time updates, static mode read-only support. API client adds fetchTriageRecords, createTriageRecord, overrideTriageRecord, actOnTriageRecord. Types in lib/types/triage.ts. Nav links in Sidebar and MobileNav. 18 tests covering all 8 own ACs + 3 trait ACs. Local review findings addressed (typed return, params consistency, effect cleanup). PR #455.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3FXJJ4X0RPBR4ZXWBCYJZ0\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"implement-triage-agent-export\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement Triage Agent Export\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@triage-agent-export\",\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@plan-interactive-triage-system\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #454. Shared triage export formatter in src/export/triage.ts extracted from CLI and daemon. Two formats: context (markdown) and JSON. All 4 own ACs and 6 trait ACs (@trait-json-output) covered with 18 dedicated tests. Prior review findings (2 MUST-FIX, 1 SHOULD-FIX) addressed in fix cycle.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@implement-triage-record-schema\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T20:16:10.820Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T01:05:57.250Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T01:37:07.220Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3FXJJ4C37PXQ7074M9R8QS\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T20:16:10.820Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation notes:\\n\\nExport formatter in src/lib/triage-export.ts or co-located in CLI command.\\nContext format: markdown template with per-item headers.\\nJSON format: raw TriageRecord array.\\nShared by CLI (kspec triage export) and API (GET /api/triage/export).\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ40YMEJKK4PDZ96Q312ZBVP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T01:13:51.315Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented shared triage export formatter in src/export/triage.ts. Extracted duplicated formatTriageContext() from both CLI (src/cli/commands/triage.ts) and daemon (packages/daemon/src/routes/triage.ts) into shared module. Two export formats: context (markdown) and JSON. exportTriageRecords() returns typed union. 18 dedicated tests covering all 4 own ACs (context format, JSON format, overrides, empty state) plus trait-json-output ACs (no ANSI, all data included, @ prefix refs, ISO timestamps). Updated daemon static analysis tests to verify shared formatter integration. Full suite: 3148 passed, 2 failed (pre-existing doctor flaky).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3SMTMK0VXV8N9SR3G0BMKT\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-fix-daemon-executable-build\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Fix daemon-executable bun build --compile failure\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"bun build --compile fails for the daemon package because route files use relative imports to parent packages (../../parser/index.js, ../../utils/grep.js, ../../parser/shadow.js). Bun's bundler cannot resolve these cross-package ESM imports.\\n\\nAffected route files:\\n- packages/daemon/src/routes/items.ts (line 26)\\n- packages/daemon/src/routes/validation.ts (lines 26, 33)\\n- packages/daemon/src/routes/meta.ts (line 22)\\n- packages/daemon/src/routes/tasks.ts (lines 30, 31)\\n- packages/daemon/src/routes/inbox.ts (lines 27, 28)\\n\\nTest: tests/daemon-executable.test.ts - first test fails with exit code 1 (expected 0).\\nInbox item: 01KHHJ27CE4SNQXCZDZRJCFK4M\\nSpec: @daemon-server ac-16\\n\\nPossible approaches:\\n1. Configure Bun bundler with proper package resolution/externals\\n2. Use workspace package imports (e.g., kynetic-spec/parser) instead of relative paths\\n3. Add a pre-build step that resolves/bundles parent package dependencies\\n\\nThe underlying issue is the monorepo structure - daemon lives in packages/daemon/ but imports from src/ at the repo root via relative paths.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #452. Fixed bun build --compile failure by changing the compile source from packages/daemon/src/index.ts to dist/daemon/index.ts where cross-package relative imports resolve correctly. All 3 daemon-executable tests pass. AC @daemon-server ac-16 covered.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"bug\",\n      \"daemon\",\n      \"infra\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T23:06:09.939Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T00:12:45.839Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T00:31:47.028Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3SS53VD4G4TCCVAS8FJWHF\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T23:08:31.739Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Automation eligible. This should be fixable by an agent — the root cause is well-documented (cross-package relative imports). If no fix is found after multiple attempts, block for manual handling.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3XTE1JQSJ5KGM5TEG8X1E1\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T00:19:07.954Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Root cause: bun build --compile was running from packages/daemon/ and trying to resolve relative imports (../../parser/index.js) which pointed outside the package to non-existent paths. Fix: Changed build:compile to compile from dist/daemon/index.ts (populated by npm run build:daemon) where the relative import paths correctly resolve to dist/parser/ and dist/utils/. Updated daemon package.json, build-executables.sh, and test. All 3 daemon-executable tests now pass. Full suite: 3105 passed, 1 failed (pre-existing doctor flaky test).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3SMVTJC1FFY14RAAA7K2SV\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-investigate-doctor-flaky-tests\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Investigate flaky doctor test failures\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Doctor tests (tests/parser/doctor.test.ts) have been reported as failing intermittently by agents during ralph loop sessions. The 29-test suite passes consistently in isolation but has been observed failing during automated runs.\\n\\nInvestigation needed:\\n- Reproduce the flaky failure (run test suite in loop or under load)\\n- Check for timing/race conditions (daemon status checks, file system operations)\\n- Check for test isolation issues (shared state between tests, temp dir cleanup)\\n- Review recent ralph logs or session notes for specific error messages\\n- Determine if related to daemon health check timeouts or mock reliability\\n\\nThe doctor test covers: shadow health, setup status, daemon running/unreachable/not-running, overall verdict, JSON output, exit codes. Any of these could have timing sensitivity.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #456. Root cause: getDaemonStatus() checks global PID file, not per-project. Fix: added vi.spyOn mocking in 3 daemon tests to isolate from host environment. Previous SHOULD-FIX (ac-daemon-running not testing running state) addressed. All 3168 tests pass.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 4,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"bug\",\n      \"investigation\",\n      \"testing\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T23:06:11.154Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T02:08:09.409Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T02:41:03.385Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3SS75HQBZFV2EWCBSPH7XS\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T23:08:33.841Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Automation eligible. Investigation task — agent should try to reproduce and identify the flaky condition. If unable to reproduce or diagnose after multiple attempts, block for manual handling.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ44Y2EQV8NBMWK9GAFAZA3M\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T02:23:27.192Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Root cause: getDaemonStatus() checks global PID file (~/.config/kspec/daemon.pid), not per-project. Tests asserting 'daemon not running' behavior failed when a real daemon was running on the host (e.g. during ralph loop sessions). Fix: Added vi.spyOn mocking of getDaemonStatus in 3 tests (ac-daemon-running, ac-daemon-not-running x2) to isolate from host environment, matching the pattern already used in the ac-daemon-unreachable test. Two consecutive full suite runs (3168 tests) pass cleanly.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4DH9RXVD50Q77AY0ADGM9Y\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-extract-triage-action-executor\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Extract shared triage action executor and deduplicate validActions\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Both src/cli/commands/triage.ts and packages/daemon/src/routes/triage.ts contain duplicate switch/case logic for triage action execution (promote/delete/defer/spec-gap/duplicate). PR #454 extracted the formatter but not the executor. Extract to a shared module (e.g. src/triage/actions.ts), update both consumers to import from it. Also deduplicate the validActions array (appears 3x in triage.ts plus once with skip). Extract to module-level constant or export from schema.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@triage-cli-commands\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #474. Extracted shared executeTriageAction() and VALID_ACTIONS to src/triage/ module. CLI and daemon now import from shared module instead of maintaining duplicate switch/case logic. VALID_ACTIONS derived from TriageActionSchema (single source of truth). All 17 own ACs and 6 trait ACs verified with test coverage. 3193 tests pass.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"refactor\",\n      \"triage\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T04:53:45.885Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T12:37:06.986Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T13:04:49.134Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V6W4E461NJ684CQJK2R19\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:52:44.302Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Refactor. Extract shared triage action executor from duplicate switch/case in triage.ts and daemon triage.ts. Create src/triage/actions.ts.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ58R2377P3FST33TC63R289\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T12:49:18.951Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Extracted shared triage action executor to src/triage/ module. Created 3 files: constants.ts (VALID_ACTIONS derived from TriageActionSchema), actions.ts (executeTriageAction with options-based logging), index.ts (public exports). Updated CLI (src/cli/commands/triage.ts) to import shared module — removed local executeTriageAction, replaced 3 hardcoded validActions arrays with VALID_ACTIONS. Updated daemon (packages/daemon/src/routes/triage.ts) similarly — removed local VALID_ACTIONS const and executeTriageAction function. Updated static analysis test in daemon-api-triage.test.ts to verify shared module import. Added 11 new tests in triage-actions.test.ts covering constants, all 5 action types, dry-run, and validation. All 3193 tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4DP400CH23DK5CCMC1ZWF2\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-audit-daemon-test-coverage\",\n      \"task-audit-static-analysis-tests\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Audit test suite and plan migration from static analysis to behavioral tests\",\n    \"type\": \"spike\",\n    \"description\": \"The test suite relies heavily on static analysis patterns — reading source files and checking for string patterns (e.g. expect(content).toContain(...)). This approach cannot catch runtime bugs and breaks on refactors (e.g. end-loop.test.ts had regex pattern tests that could not detect the false-positive bug that caused a real ralph loop exit).\\n\\nDeep dive:\\n1) Inventory ALL test files repo-wide and categorize by test approach (static analysis vs behavioral vs E2E).\\n2) Identify which static-only tests have the highest risk of missing real bugs.\\n3) Design a migration plan — options include: unit tests that import functions directly, integration tests with fixtures, CLI behavioral tests, or Playwright E2E tests.\\n4) Create follow-up tasks for the actual migration work.\\n\\nKnown areas with static analysis tests:\\n- Daemon tests (tests/daemon-*.test.ts)\\n- Ralph end-loop tests (tests/ralph/end-loop.test.ts) — session close handlers, marker removal\\n- Likely others across the test suite\\n\\nThe pattern to eliminate: reading source with fs.readFile then expect(content).toContain(...)\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Audit complete. Identified ~3,500 lines of static analysis tests across 14 files covering ~98 ACs. Created 10 follow-up tasks: 9 E2E replacement tasks for daemon APIs and 1 deletion task for tests that don't need replacing. All tasks are automation-eligible with concrete endpoints, AC annotations, and file references.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"testing\",\n      \"daemon\",\n      \"e2e\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T04:56:23.808Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-25T23:43:23.129Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-25T23:46:10.108Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-26T00:29:20.781Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V7Q7CK4JF2GTV37NGWNQD\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:53:12.044Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"MANUAL_ONLY: Spike requiring human investigation and judgment for test migration plan.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ9ZWGGPGFRQWTCBDNCR0Z0H\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-25T08:50:39.766Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Session audit 01KJ8Z3Q identified additional static analysis tests to include: (1) end-loop.test.ts lines 255-372 — 5 tests reading ralph.ts source for string patterns (ac-detect, session close handlers, ac-remove-markers), (2) session-budget-integration.test.ts lines 295-339 — marker code removal tests reading ralph.ts source. Both files already have behavioral equivalents alongside the static ones, so migration = delete static tests after confirming behavioral coverage.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJBK313W12Q9TCXPF8X620QH\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-25T23:45:30.749Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUDIT COMPLETE — Inventory of static analysis tests across the repo:\\n\\n**7 files with static analysis patterns, ~59 total tests.**\\n\\nHIGH RISK (P1):\\n- daemon-server.test.ts: ~13 tests read packages/daemon/src/server.ts and check string patterns for port, hostname, health, CORS, signals, WebSocket. Zero runtime verification of daemon behavior.\\n- ralph/end-loop.test.ts lines 254-372: 8 tests read src/cli/commands/ralph.ts checking session state detection, signal handlers, session close paths, marker removal. Already known to miss real bugs (false-positive end-loop exit bug).\\n\\nMEDIUM RISK (P2):\\n- ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts lines 293-339: 13 tests checking marker code removal (26 patterns). Absence tests.\\n- normalize-ref-input.test.ts lines 55-139: 8 tests doing lint-style anti-pattern detection on CLI commands and daemon routes.\\n- skill-module-split.test.ts lines 18-69: 6 tests checking file existence and string patterns. Same file has good behavioral tests on lines 74-120.\\n- web-ui-shared-types.test.ts: 5 tests checking re-export patterns in type files.\\n\\nLOW RISK (P3):\\n- package-distribution.test.ts: 6 tests checking template file content patterns.\\n\\nMIGRATION APPROACHES:\\n1. daemon-server → E2E Playwright tests hitting actual endpoints\\n2. ralph end-loop/session-budget → Import functions directly, unit test logic\\n3. normalize-ref-input → ESLint custom rule or keep as lint-like\\n4. skill-module-split → Convert to import-based checks (already partially done)\\n5. web-ui-shared-types → TypeScript import verification\\n6. package-distribution → npm pack --dry-run for realistic verification\\n\\n~40+ other files use readFile legitimately (reading test output, YAML fixtures, etc.)\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJBNK3GGD5D43GD8G7WTHM1W\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T00:29:14.640Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUDIT RESTRUCTURED — Original 4 tasks deleted, replaced with 10 properly-scoped tasks:\\n\\nE2E REPLACEMENT TASKS (9 tasks, P2):\\n- @task-e2e-daemon-tasks-api — replace daemon-api-tasks.test.ts (258 lines, @api-contract ac-2 through ac-7)\\n- @task-e2e-daemon-items-api — replace daemon-api-items.test.ts (217 lines, @api-contract ac-8 through ac-11)\\n- @task-e2e-daemon-inbox-api — replace daemon-api-inbox.test.ts (218 lines, @api-contract ac-12 through ac-14)\\n- @task-e2e-daemon-meta-validation-api — replace daemon-api-meta.test.ts + daemon-api-validation.test.ts (390 lines, @api-contract ac-15 through ac-21)\\n- @task-e2e-daemon-triage-api — replace daemon-api-triage.test.ts (414 lines, @triage-daemon-api ac-1 through ac-9)\\n- @task-e2e-daemon-errors-projects-api — replace daemon-api-error-handling.test.ts + daemon-api-projects.test.ts (383 lines, @api-contract ac-22-24, @multi-directory-daemon ac-28-30)\\n- @task-e2e-daemon-server-core — replace daemon-server.test.ts static parts (310 lines, @daemon-server ac-11,15, @api-contract ac-1)\\n- @task-e2e-daemon-websocket — replace daemon-websocket.test.ts (591 lines, @api-contract ac-25-33, @trait-websocket-protocol)\\n- @task-e2e-daemon-watcher — replace daemon-watcher.test.ts (163 lines, @daemon-server ac-4-6)\\n\\nDELETION TASK (1 task, P2):\\n- @task-delete-static-analysis-tests — delete skill-module-split, web-ui-shared-types, web-ui-triage, plus partial cleanup of end-loop, normalize-ref-input, package-distribution\\n\\nKey decisions:\\n- All daemon API tests become Playwright E2E hitting real daemon (not vitest static analysis)\\n- skill-module-split tests deleted entirely (one-time refactoring outcome, not ongoing behavior)\\n- web-ui-shared-types deleted (convention enforcement, not behavior)\\n- normalize-ref-input anti-pattern scanning deleted (not worth ESLint rule)\\n- Ralph absence tests (removed markers) kept — static scanning IS the right tool for absence checks\\n- Localhost middleware unit tests kept — already behavioral\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"manual_only\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4F7XFGJVY44SC1KA0FQMAD\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-deduplicate-web-ui-types\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Eliminate duplicated types in web-ui by importing from shared schema\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"packages/web-ui/src/lib/types/triage.ts manually mirrors types from src/schema/triage.ts. If the schema changes, web-ui types silently diverge. The codebase has @kynetic-ai/shared for shared types (already imported in api.ts), but triage types bypass this. Scope: 1) Audit all packages/web-ui/src/lib/types/ files for types that duplicate src/schema/ definitions. 2) For each duplicated type, determine if it can be imported from the shared package or needs a re-export. 3) Migrate triage types and any other duplicates to use the shared source of truth. 4) Add a lint rule or CI check to prevent future type duplication.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #475. Added 10 types to @kynetic-ai/shared (Convention, TriageStatus, TriageAction, TriageRecord, ExportedTask, ExportedItem, InheritedAC, ExportedValidation, KspecSnapshot, ExportedProject). Replaced web-ui types/triage.ts and types/snapshot.ts with re-exports from shared. Added static analysis test preventing future type drift. Fixed Convention.validation to match actual schema per Codex review. All 3196 tests pass, all CI checks green.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"refactor\",\n      \"web-ui\",\n      \"types\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T05:23:35.534Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T13:05:20.590Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T13:29:39.033Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V5EXY9MKMZY4J2EY5RBG8\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:51:58.014Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Standalone refactor. Audit packages/web-ui/src/lib/types/ for duplicated src/schema/ types. Import from @kynetic-ai/shared instead.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5AASG9GFP45J1HX6PS4N1F\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T13:17:01.321Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Audited packages/web-ui/src/lib/types/ and found 4 clear duplicates (TriageStatus, TriageAction, TriageRecord, Convention) plus 5 types (ExportedTask, ExportedItem, InheritedAC, ExportedValidation, KspecSnapshot) duplicated from src/export/types.ts. Added all missing types to @kynetic-ai/shared api.ts. Replaced both web-ui types files with re-exports from shared. Added static analysis test (web-ui-shared-types.test.ts) that enforces no local interface/type definitions in the types directory. Updated existing web-ui-triage.test.ts to verify re-export pattern. All 3196 tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4FT9A2KX5103BTEWYT143V\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-fix-sidebar-nav-links\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Fix web UI sidebar navigation links not clickable\",\n    \"type\": \"bug\",\n    \"description\": \"SidebarMenuButton renders a <button> element, not an <a>. When Sidebar.svelte passes href, the href lands on a button (which browsers ignore). Result: Dashboard, Tasks, Items, Inbox, Triage links are all dead — only Observations works because it uses onclick with goto(). Fix: either use the child snippet pattern to render an <a> tag, or add onclick handlers with goto() like Observations does. Also add /triage to the spaRoutes array in packages/daemon/src/server.ts line 338 so the daemon serves index.html for the triage route.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #457. Fixed sidebar nav links by using shadcn-svelte child snippet pattern to render <a> elements instead of dead <button> elements. Added /triage to daemon SPA fallback routes. User manually verified links work and triage page renders.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"web-ui\",\n      \"bug\",\n      \"navigation\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T05:33:37.467Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T05:34:14.754Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T05:59:50.617Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4GA9BVH2M2SSZADS3EP7C3\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T05:42:21.819Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Fixed two issues: 1) Sidebar nav links were rendering as <button> elements instead of <a> tags. SidebarMenuButton from shadcn-svelte renders a button by default — used the child snippet pattern to render proper <a> elements with href. 2) Added /triage to daemon SPA fallback routes in server.ts so direct URL navigation works. Full test suite passes (3167/3167 + 3 skipped, 1 pre-existing flaky test in batch-exec-engine unrelated to changes).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4FTAE506Y45KTGFMFB57NQ\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-redesign-web-ui\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Redesign web UI holistically — interactive spec/design session\",\n    \"type\": \"spike\",\n    \"description\": \"The current web UI has fundamental issues beyond individual bugs: sidebar nav links are dead buttons, SPA fallback routes must be manually maintained, daemon test coverage is static-only, types are duplicated between web-ui and schema. Before fixing piecemeal, do a holistic redesign session to: 1) Inventory what currently exists and works. 2) Define what the web UI should actually be. 3) Choose a component architecture that works. 4) Spec out the redesigned UI with acceptance criteria. 5) Create a plan with prioritized tasks. This should be an interactive session with the user.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"web-ui\",\n      \"design\",\n      \"spike\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T05:33:38.629Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V7SENBYDYV28R1CT2910G\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:53:14.325Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"MANUAL_ONLY: Spike requiring interactive design session with user.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"manual_only\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4HJB047Y2M2NJ54YJBJCJJ\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-update-triage-skill\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Update triage skill to use new kspec triage CLI commands\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"The /triage skill (.claude/skills/triage/SKILL.md) predates the triage record system implemented in PRs #449-455. It still references the old manual flow (kspec inbox delete/promote) without mentioning kspec triage record, kspec triage start, kspec triage act, kspec triage export, or the triage record lifecycle. Update the skill to: 1) Incorporate kspec triage start for interactive triage sessions. 2) Replace manual inbox promote/delete flows with kspec triage record + kspec triage act two-step pattern. 3) Document kspec triage export for agent handoff context. 4) Update the inbox sub-doc (docs/inbox.md) accordingly. 5) Ensure the skill teaches agents the full triage record workflow (record → act, override flow, export for context).\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@triage-cli-commands\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #458. Updated triage skill with record→act workflow, added as core skill in templates/skills/, extended install/update/build to copy supporting dirs recursively with ENOENT-only error handling. Tests added for all new behavior.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"skill\",\n      \"triage\",\n      \"docs\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T06:04:14.212Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T06:19:49.195Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T06:59:04.141Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4JAVPGR8HX3KYBFX9JDP5N\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T06:17:37.744Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Updated triage skill with new record→act workflow. Made it a core skill in templates/skills/triage/ with SKILL.md + docs/ (inbox.md, observations.md, automation.md). Extended core skill install/update/build-plugin to copy supporting directories (docs/, references/, scripts/, assets/) not just SKILL.md. Updated @core-skill-install ac-2 and @core-skill-update ac-1 specs to cover supporting files. All tests pass (182 skill tests + 3 setup tests).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4JEPSZHR36BAR5K8KZQXF8\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T06:19:43.808Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Reset from completed to pending\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4K2HVFYS4M3XQCCP426DTP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T06:30:34.095Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"PR #458 created (feat/triage-core-skill). Awaiting CI and review. All work complete: skill content updated, core template created, install/update/build extended for supporting dirs, project-level skill removed, specs updated.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4PEV6Q2D7QHS2SNPRDCG3Y\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Regenerate kspec-agents.md after release version bump\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"The release skill should run 'kspec agents generate' after the version bump PR is merged, so the kspec-agents.md header version stays in sync. Add as a post-release step in Phase 7 or 8 of the release skill.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #477. Added kspec agents generate step to release skill Phase 6. After npm version bumps package.json, the skill regenerates kspec-agents.md so the version header stays in sync. Updated dry-run preview and Phase 8 report checklist. Addressed Codex review: added inline comment about using npm run dev -- for self-hosting releases. All CI checks pass.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"release\",\n      \"agents\",\n      \"improvement\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T07:29:42.615Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T14:01:56.972Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T14:29:03.740Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V5G3FFRM227ADDRT8JJZX\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:51:59.215Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Standalone chore. Add kspec agents generate as post-release step in release skill. Keeps kspec-agents.md version in sync.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5D53YVAXNVW861FVN8X0NF\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T14:06:21.148Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Added kspec agents generate step to release skill Phase 6. After npm version bumps package.json, the skill now regenerates kspec-agents.md before committing — so the tagged commit includes the updated version header. Also updated the dry-run preview actions list and Phase 8 report checklist to include the regeneration step. Added note about self-hosting projects needing npm run dev -- agents generate. All 3201 tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4Q55END42JJK7TVXP5WT88\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Add path-based CI test filtering\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Configure CI to only run the test suite when files that affect test outcomes are changed. Use GitHub Actions path filters to skip tests for documentation-only, skill-only, or other non-code changes.\\n\\nApproach: Define paths that trigger tests (src/**, tests/**, packages/**, package.json, etc.) rather than paths that skip tests. This is safer — new code paths get tested by default.\\n\\nExamples of changes that should skip tests:\\n- .claude/skills/**\\n- docs/**\\n- templates/agents-sections/**\\n- *.md (except possibly SKILL.md files that get loaded at runtime — evaluate)\\n- .kspec/**\\n\\nConsider: GitHub Actions path filtering with paths/paths-ignore on the test job.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #461. Added path-based filtering to CI test workflow.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"ci\",\n      \"improvement\",\n      \"infra\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T07:41:53.997Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T07:42:24.427Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:00:33.185Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4Q8RVED8PFNJV08G63ZGJX\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T07:43:52.174Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"PR #461 created with path-based filtering. Tests only run on PRs when code-relevant files change. Awaiting CI pass and merge.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SM4DTQA7D7GE81GARBBX6\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Error message consistency: task needs-work uses inline error string instead of centralized error str\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Error message consistency: task needs-work uses inline error string instead of centralized error strings pattern (src/strings/errors.ts). Should add cannotNeedsWork or similar to match cannotStart pattern.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #478. Centralized inline error strings in task needs-work handler to errors.ts: added cannotNeedsWork to statusErrors and needsWorkTask to operationFailures. Also fixed flaky CI test by bumping timeout on full fix cycle round-trip test. All CI checks pass.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:25:01.626Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T14:29:16.427Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T14:54:28.132Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V5H9V3JMF85W753X7ZSDF\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:52:00.443Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Bug fix. Move inline error string to src/strings/errors.ts following cannotStart pattern. Update task needs-work handler.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5EREMKFZCE2GPF47FZ8CBF\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T14:34:23.252Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Moved inline error string from task needs-work handler to centralized errors.ts. Added cannotNeedsWork to statusErrors and needsWorkTask to operationFailures. Updated task.ts handler to use errors.status.cannotNeedsWork() and errors.failures.needsWorkTask. All 3201 tests pass including the existing needs-work error message assertions.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SM5NXME299C3KB4FG7J0A\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Input ref normalization layer: Add normalizeRefInput() in schema/common.ts that ensures @ prefix on \",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Input ref normalization layer: Add normalizeRefInput() in schema/common.ts that ensures @ prefix on ref-like strings. Apply at CLI input boundary (TaskInput construction) instead of per-command handler. Prevents class of bugs where bare refs bypass RefSchema validation and cause silent data loss. Today's depends_on fix (PR #353) patched 3 locations — a shared boundary would prevent recurrence. Related: @merge-ref-normalization (merge layer), @01KG0N4V (silent safeParse drops).\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #479. Added normalizeRefInput() in schema/common.ts, replaced 10 inline ref normalization patterns across 8 files. Added 13 tests (6 unit, 2 static analysis regression guards, 5 integration). All quality gates passed.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:25:02.909Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T14:56:25.606Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T15:31:15.039Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V6BYWSR59V1DADTDGHMSR\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:52:27.740Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Standalone refactor. Add normalizeRefInput() in schema/common.ts ensuring @ prefix at CLI boundary. Prevents recurring bare ref bugs.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5GGQVX4QPP8PG6W8SXCAF6\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T15:05:07.710Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Added normalizeRefInput() to schema/common.ts. Replaced all 10 inline ref normalization patterns across 7 files: task.ts, derive.ts, plan-import.ts, meta.ts, log.ts, triage.ts (CLI), triage.ts (daemon routes). Also normalized spec_ref, meta_ref, plan_ref fields in task add/set which were previously un-normalized. 13 new tests: 6 unit tests for the function, 2 static analysis preventing regression, 5 integration tests verifying imports. All 3214 tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SM6RN06C487QWRWABJ86J\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"kspec plan import should place type:trait items with no parent in the project-level traits array (ky\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"kspec plan import should place type:trait items with no parent in the project-level traits array (kynetic.yaml), not the module-level traits array. Currently causes schema validation error.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #480. Fixed plan import to place type:trait items with no parent in kynetic.yaml project-level traits array instead of module-level traits. Implementation mirrors existing kspec trait add pattern. AC coverage: ac-11 (trait creation), ac-15 (dry-run output). All tests pass.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:25:04.021Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T15:33:53.291Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T15:57:26.853Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V6QNYAEW0WWCY7KNABP51\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:52:39.742Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Enhancement. Traits without parent go to kynetic.yaml project-level traits array, not module-level. Spec @plan-import.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5JDY5RRD251M1BVMQ7E434\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T15:38:33.017Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Fixed trait placement in plan import. When a spec has type:trait and no parent, it now writes directly to kynetic.yaml project-level traits array (same path as kspec trait add) instead of going through addChildItem which placed it in the module-level traits array. Added 3 tests: parentless trait goes to kynetic.yaml, trait with parent stays in module file, dry-run reports project-level trait placement. All 3222 tests pass (1 pre-existing timeout in cli-serve unrelated).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SM7SSXD7S0ZN6VDXTDD85\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"kspec item add needs --root flag for adding traits to project-level kynetic.yaml without --under. Cu\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"kspec item add needs --root flag for adding traits to project-level kynetic.yaml without --under. Currently impossible via CLI, requiring manual YAML edits that violate the never-edit-manually rule.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:25:05.081Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V7KPFGSXBBGSXS5KP4VCC\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:53:08.431Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Automation status set to needs_review: Spec gap - @item-add has no --root flag AC. Need to update spec before implementing.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V7MXQDDPGFQGFCP91VM11\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:53:09.687Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"NEEDS_REVIEW: @item-add spec documents --parent and --type but has no --root flag for placing traits in kynetic.yaml. Add AC to @item-add before implementing.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"needs_review\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SM8TEBGJ7WXRTTVQKTY3S\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"kspec-agents.md Finding Information table shows skill IDs as /help instead of /kspec:help — generate\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"kspec-agents.md Finding Information table shows skill IDs as /help instead of /kspec:help — generateSkillsTable() in agent-data-sections.ts doesn't account for namespace rendering of core skills\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Already implemented. generateSkillsTable() in agent-data-sections.ts already handles core skill namespace at line 42: skill.origin === 'core' produces /kspec:<id> invocation. Tests at lines 114-146 verify core vs project skill rendering. kspec agents generate --dry-run confirms all 11 core skills render with /kspec: prefix. 28 tests pass.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:25:06.126Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T15:57:59.979Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T15:59:32.185Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V6D4491AMKWWJKJX309AS\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:52:28.933Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Bug fix. Fix generateSkillsTable() in agent-data-sections.ts to render core skill IDs with kspec: namespace prefix. Spec @agent-instruction-gen.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SM9TQ4TMDAZ5HHY0PDS94\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"task complete --force should bypass the submit requirement. Currently --force does not skip the in_p\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"task complete --force should bypass the submit requirement. Currently --force does not skip the in_progress → pending_review transition, making it impossible to complete non-code tasks (design, triage, research) without a meaningless submit step. The --force flag exists but does not actually force completion from in_progress state.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #481. --force flag now bypasses all state checks in task complete, enabling direct completion from in_progress, pending, blocked, and cancelled states. Documents prior state in note and warning. 7 tests cover all force-complete paths. Spec @task-commands ac-1 fully covered.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:25:07.159Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T16:01:14.301Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T16:24:01.884Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V6E89ZPNTQDCYEM89V20W\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:52:30.089Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Enhancement. --force flag should bypass submit requirement for direct completion from in_progress. Spec @task-complete.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5M15A7AYHWWY32A14NC2QH\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T16:06:31.495Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Fixed --force to bypass ALL state checks in task complete, not just blocked. Changed forcingBlockedTask to forcingCompletion (options.force). Updated note generation to document prior state for any non-pending_review force completion. Updated warning output similarly. Added 5 new tests: force from in_progress, pending, cancelled, already-completed guard, and pending_review no-op. All 3225 tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SMATMC7TD3H0C2S5K9W4T\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"kspec batch cannot handle task patch with nested --data JSON argument. The data object gets stringif\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"kspec batch cannot handle task patch with nested --data JSON argument. The data object gets stringified as [object Object] instead of being serialized as JSON. Batch args are likely passed through a simple string coercion. Workaround: run task patch commands individually. Fix: batch arg handling should JSON.stringify objects before passing to command handlers.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #482. Fixed batch arg serialization to JSON.stringify nested objects instead of String() which produced [object Object]. Added toArgString() helper, comprehensive tests including trait AC coverage, and dry_run boolean field to BatchExecResult.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:25:08.180Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T18:51:05.986Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T21:38:31.682Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V6FEHNKAMR2A4CFZ6WQ6W\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:52:31.313Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Bug fix. Batch arg handling should JSON.stringify objects before passing to handlers. Spec @batch-exec.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5NG687NCF4GAAGASEY2PDK\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T16:32:12.551Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Added toArgString() helper in batch-exec.ts that JSON.stringify objects instead of using String() which produces [object Object]. Fix applied to all 4 value-serialization paths in buildCommandArgv (positional scalars, positional array items, option scalars, option array items). 3 unit tests + 1 integration test with real task patch through batch. All 3229 tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5P5HSH0F936M14PD9724WJ\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T16:43:52.498Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: Re-review: Previous findings unaddressed (same HEAD e30e7dd). MUST-FIX: trait AC coverage annotations missing for @batch-exec inherited traits (@trait-json-output, @trait-semantic-exit-codes, @trait-error-guidance, @trait-dry-run, @trait-shadow-commit). SHOULD-FIX: new regression tests lack // AC: annotations. No new commits since last review — worker must address findings before merge.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5PKD8XB2XFGWNMP4E8MGXW\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T16:51:26.621Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Addressed review findings: added // AC: annotations for all 5 inherited traits (@trait-json-output, @trait-semantic-exit-codes, @trait-error-guidance, @trait-dry-run, @trait-shadow-commit). Added 6 new dedicated trait AC tests covering JSON ref prefix, ISO 8601 timestamps, JSON error guidance, runtime exit codes, dry-run error handling, and dry-run field. Annotated existing regression test. All 3235 tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5WJFJ724ZG9X1V0RHFJMCY\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T18:35:47.655Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 3] Review findings: Audit findings: (1) Unresolved review thread on GitHub blocks check-unresolved-comments CI. (2) Weak trait AC test @trait-json-output ac-4 - assertion checks command name not @ prefix on refs. (3) Weak trait AC test @trait-dry-run ac-6 - checks string 'dry-run' not actual dry_run boolean field. Strengthen or remove those 2 annotations, resolve the GH thread, then resubmit.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5XEJR8C7BGYM4DK48Y4CZS\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T18:51:08.425Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 4] Addressed review findings: (1) Added dry_run: true boolean field to BatchExecResult type and dry-run response path, satisfying @trait-dry-run ac-6. Strengthened test to assert actual boolean instead of string. (2) Removed misleading @trait-json-output ac-4 annotation — batch JSON envelope doesn't contain entity references. (3) Resolved GitHub review thread PRRT_kwDOQ7Tfmc5wLbCc. All 3233 tests pass (1 pre-existing cli-serve flake).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SMBV2YAJV75E3Y7VWQ4NZ\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Bug: `kspec plan import` ignores spec_ref on manual tasks. AC @plan-import ac-27 says manual tasks g\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Bug: `kspec plan import` ignores spec_ref on manual tasks. AC @plan-import ac-27 says manual tasks get no spec_ref, but when a task YAML explicitly provides spec_ref pointing to a valid spec, it should be honored. Currently taskDef.spec_ref is never read in the manual task creation path (plan-import.ts:513-523).\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #483. Honors spec_ref on manual tasks in plan import. All CI green, audit confirmed clean.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:25:09.218Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T16:52:10.116Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T18:35:59.940Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V6GP4P30YKMGXRHV7KN5N\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:52:32.580Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Bug fix. Fix plan-import.ts:513-523 to read taskDef.spec_ref in manual task creation path. Spec @plan-import.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5Q6CN255BB7VBYHJ4VY2EH\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T17:01:48.578Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Added spec_ref field to PlanTaskSchema and honored it in plan-import manual task creation path. Uses normalizeRefInput for @ prefix normalization. Updated AC ac-27 to reflect the new behavior. 2 new tests: explicit spec_ref honored, bare ref normalized. All 3227 tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SMCWBGEWF6MD1VS0AS0JH\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Bug: `kspec session start --json` (and other --json commands) mix info lines (ℹ Synced shadow branch\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Bug: `kspec session start --json` (and other --json commands) mix info lines (ℹ Synced shadow branch) into stdout, breaking JSON parsing. Info/sync messages should go to stderr when --json mode is active.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #476. Fixed info/warning messages leaking into stdout in --json mode by routing them through info()/warn() helpers that send to stderr in structured output modes. 5 new tests covering JSON purity, static analysis, and YAML mode. All quality gates passed.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:25:10.283Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T13:31:39.345Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T14:01:26.928Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V6HYH3XMMRRRKMM3S4XX0\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:52:33.873Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Bug fix. Route info/sync messages to stderr when --json mode active. Spec @cmd-session-start. Check trait @trait-json-output.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5BKAPS3M06XE1YM0BFEF7E\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T13:39:09.657Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Fixed info/warning messages leaking into stdout in --json mode. Replaced raw console.log() calls in sessionStartAction() with info()/warn() from output.ts which suppress output in structured modes. Added 3 tests: static analysis verifying no raw console.log in action handler, runtime test verifying valid JSON on stdout, and test verifying no info/warning markers in stdout. All 3199 tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SNECVEF1DWQTDK9KK5ASN\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"task set --spec-ref has no way to clear the field. --plan-ref supports 'null' to clear but --spec-re\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"task set --spec-ref has no way to clear the field. --plan-ref supports 'null' to clear but --spec-ref tries to resolve 'null' as a reference. Should support same 'null' pattern for consistency. Workaround: find an alternative valid spec reference to link to.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #490. Added null clearing support for --spec-ref and --meta-ref in task set, matching existing --plan-ref behavior. All ACs covered with annotated tests, CI green.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:25:44.603Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-24T01:51:33.450Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T02:12:44.599Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V6K555PGCK411D7FGZRNP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:52:35.109Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Bug fix. Support null value for --spec-ref to clear field, matching --plan-ref behavior. Spec @task-set.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5R7C67Q326FWMBB5EWW6HC\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T17:19:49.447Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Session audit: This task was started in the final iteration of ralph loop session 01KJ4VNM but the session ended immediately after. No code changes, branches, or work exist for this task. Needs to be picked up fresh in a future session.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5WJMWACCXGAQBAK84VHYQ8\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T18:35:53.098Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Reset from in_progress to pending\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6NXS5CQY86VP9QTMPTD8XC\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T01:58:52.332Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented null clearing for --spec-ref and --meta-ref in task set command, matching existing --plan-ref behavior. Added ac-clear-ref to @task-set spec. All 3255 tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SNFKB1FKXDGWAJB5Q1V23\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"plan import: add depends_on field to plan YAML spec format so specs/tasks get structural dependencie\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"plan import: add depends_on field to plan YAML spec format so specs/tasks get structural dependencies on import. Currently plan import creates specs and tasks but dependencies must be added manually post-import. Add a depends_on param per spec entry in the YAML (e.g., depends_on: [@full-model-recipe]) that maps to spec depends_on and task blocked_by on import.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@plan-import\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #491. Added depends_on field to plan import YAML format for both specs and tasks. Two-pass spec→task slug mapping resolves dependencies correctly including mixed imports (new specs depending on existing specs). 7 new tests, all CI passing.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:25:45.835Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-24T02:13:12.913Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T02:43:31.631Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V6M9EBMSQ6M9FY6B8H7HD\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:52:36.270Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Enhancement. Add depends_on to plan YAML spec format. Parse per spec entry, map to spec depends_on and task blocked_by. Spec @plan-import.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6Q9HNNJ8YV0Y51J9NYY776\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T02:22:46.453Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Added depends_on field to PlanSpecSchema and PlanTaskSchema. Plan import now: (1) maps spec depends_on to created spec depends_on fields with @ normalization, (2) resolves spec depends_on to derived task depends_on using spec→task slug mapping, (3) passes depends_on through on manual tasks. Added ac-35 to @plan-import. 7 new tests (2 parser, 5 CLI integration). All 3262 tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SNGM76D56HTXHR6HQ02E2\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Plan import should support task priority: plan document specs can specify priority, and derived task\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Plan import should support task priority: plan document specs can specify priority, and derived tasks should inherit it. Currently all derived tasks get P3 regardless of plan content. Workaround: manually batch-set priorities after import.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@plan-import\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #492. Plan import now supports priority field on specs (1-5), derived tasks inherit priority from their source spec, defaulting to P3 when unspecified.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:25:46.887Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-24T02:43:57.817Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T03:02:53.550Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V6NCVG3QRN04CBACDYRWE\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:52:37.404Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Enhancement. Plan specs specify priority, derived tasks inherit instead of defaulting P3. Spec @plan-import.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6RSB1074YK4MTQAXK041YQ\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T02:48:52.512Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Added priority field to PlanSpecSchema (int 1-5, optional). Derived tasks now inherit priority from their source plan spec (planSpec?.priority ?? 3) instead of hardcoded 3. Manual tasks already supported priority. Added ac-36 to @plan-import. 1 new parser test + 4 new CLI integration tests covering: inheritance, range support, manual task independence, and schema validation of out-of-range values.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SNHRE8SZT8NG5N9K8ENV9\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"kspec plan import should detect and report YAML-unsafe values in AC fields (colons in then: values) \",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"kspec plan import should detect and report YAML-unsafe values in AC fields (colons in then: values) before attempting parse, rather than failing with cryptic nested mapping error.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #493. Plan import now detects YAML-unsafe values (unquoted colons) in AC fields and provides diagnostic hints with field name, line number, and fix suggestion (use block scalars). Applied to both Specs and Tasks YAML parsing. Added detectYamlUnsafeValues() utility, ac-37 to @plan-import. 9 unit tests + 1 CLI integration test. Codex review finding (list marker prefix) addressed.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:25:48.046Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-24T03:03:26.638Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T03:22:16.157Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V6PJ0QZ0F1XQ9MNAKRAVV\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:52:38.592Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Improvement. Detect YAML-unsafe values in AC fields before parse. Provide clear diagnostic instead of cryptic error. Spec @plan-import.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6T0XC3QS051BWQE3AA7DHT\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T03:10:29.251Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented YAML-unsafe value detection for plan import. When YAML parsing fails due to unquoted colons in AC fields (given/when/then/description), the error now includes diagnostic hints identifying the specific field, line number, and problematic value, plus a fix suggestion to use block scalars. Added detectYamlUnsafeValues() to plan-document.ts (exported for testing). Diagnostics applied to both Specs and Tasks section parsing. Added ac-37 to @plan-import. 8 new parser tests + 1 CLI integration test.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4T45FMV4TV07MWX7RNA8F8\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Bug: kspec task add returned OK with ULID but task was not findable via task get or tasks list. Had \",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Bug: kspec task add returned OK with ULID but task was not findable via task get or tasks list. Had to retry to get a persistent task. Possible shadow branch commit race condition or ULID issue. Observed during session 2026-02-22.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #494. Added advisory file locking (mkdir-based) to all 10 YAML mutation functions to prevent concurrent write data loss. Consolidated duplicate lock from plans.ts. 9 tests covering lock mechanics and concurrent safety.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:33:46.996Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-24T03:22:46.028Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T04:04:07.417Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V6RRKKPMW0A8VY6MHGFYX\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:52:40.851Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Bug investigation. task add returned OK but task not findable. Investigate shadow branch commit race condition or ULID collision.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6VB9MD2MQBFJYNFFRYA7GS\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T03:33:38.061Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Root cause: non-atomic read-modify-write in saveTask and other YAML mutation functions. When concurrent kspec processes write to the same file (common in ralph loop), second write can overwrite first. Fix: extracted advisory file lock (mkdir-based, with PID + timestamp stale detection) into src/parser/file-lock.ts. Applied to: saveTask, deleteTask, saveInboxItem, deleteInboxItem, saveTriageRecord, addChildItem, updateSpecItem, deleteSpecItem, savePlan, deletePlan. Consolidated duplicate lock in plans.ts. 7 unit tests for lock mechanism including concurrent write safety.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4T46TRY4JSDJW2WBEY8Z6B\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Codex skill prompt needs ralph-loop safety guard. During ralph loop session 01KJ3N2N8V38823H87PG09V7\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Codex skill prompt needs ralph-loop safety guard. During ralph loop session 01KJ3N2N8V38823H87PG09V7XR, the worker agent invoked /codex review #448 (per focus instructions). The codex agent (gpt-5.3-codex, danger-full-access sandbox) ran a 'CLI spot-check' that accidentally started a kspec ralph process, then ran pkill -f 'kspec ralph' to clean it up — which killed the actual ralph loop process hosting it. Codex session rollout-2026-02-22T14-02-07 completed normally (703k tokens, clean exit) while ralph died mid-tool-call (session stuck at active, no session.end event, last event seq 963 was the codex exec Bash call). Fix: add context to the codex skill prompt when invoked inside ralph (e.g. 'You are running inside a kspec ralph loop. NEVER start kspec ralph, kspec serve, or use pkill/kill on kspec processes.'). Could detect ralph context via KSPEC_SESSION_ID env var or similar. Alternative: restrict sandbox mode when codex is called from ralph. See codex skill at .claude/skills/codex/SKILL.md and ralph tool handler at src/cli/commands/ralph.ts:589-634.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #495. Added ralph-loop safety guard to codex skill: (1) ralph sets KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION env var on process.env so all spawned agents (worker, subagent, wrap-up) inherit it, (2) codex SKILL.md has new safety guard section with detection and preamble instructions preventing Codex from starting/killing kspec processes. Mock ACP extended with env verification. 2 tests. Codex review findings addressed (env propagation to subagents, improved negative test).\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:33:48.376Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-24T04:04:39.622Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T04:26:47.848Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V6SVB6VCEA2G1YK0FFET2\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:52:41.963Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Safety chore. Add ralph-loop context to codex skill prompt. Detect via KSPEC_SESSION_ID env var. Prevent kspec ralph/serve/pkill from inside codex.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6XJYT6BHCVAXTHZ7AF1YKR\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T04:12:46.279Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Added ralph-loop safety guard to codex skill. Two changes: (1) ralph.ts now passes KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION=<sessionId> env var to spawned agents via spawnAndInitialize. (2) Codex SKILL.md has new 'Ralph Loop Safety Guard' section with detection logic (env var primary, marker files fallback) and safety preamble that must be prepended to all codex prompts when inside ralph. Mock ACP extended with env var verification (MOCK_ACP_VERIFY_ENV_FILE/MOCK_ACP_VERIFY_ENV_VARS). 2 new tests verify env propagation.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4T480J60WY0ESJWQY08G82\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"kspec batch silently fails on malformed JSON input - exits with code 1 and no error message. Should \",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"kspec batch silently fails on malformed JSON input - exits with code 1 and no error message. Should print JSON parse error or validation error details. batch has did-you-mean for bad arg keys (PR #440) but nothing for structural JSON errors. Encountered during triage session when batch --commands failed with no diagnostic output.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #496. Test-only changes: strengthened batch malformed JSON error tests to verify error message content (position info) not just exit codes, added JSON-mode structured error test, added non-array valid JSON schema validation test, fixed AC annotation prefixes.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:33:49.586Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-24T04:27:39.693Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T05:06:20.414Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4V6V0HXEDTJM35H285YYMG\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:52:43.153Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"AUTOMATION: Bug fix. Surface JSON parse error details on malformed input. AC @batch-exec ac-invalid-json requires error with line/position info. Currently silent.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ7054ZJKQD1Q5WS1AQDXA1K\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T04:57:39.570Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Investigated the bug: error handling code is already in place and working. Malformed JSON produces clear error messages with position info (e.g., 'Invalid JSON: Expected property name at position 1 (line 1 column 2)'). The original issue may have been transient or occurred during concurrent operations. Strengthened existing tests: (1) integration test now verifies error message content (position info) not just exit code, (2) added JSON-mode error test verifying structured {success,error} output, (3) added non-array valid JSON test for schema validation path, (4) strengthened empty batch test to verify error message. All 3295 tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5WV0G52E3BZA5W3VPW22J1\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Fix ralph event logging iteration capture-by-value bug\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"In ralph.ts:1573-1579, the streaming update event handler fires appendEvent() without await (fire-and-forget). The iteration variable is captured by closure reference, not by value. By the time the async callback executes, iteration has already been incremented in the for loop — so hundreds of tool_call events get tagged with the wrong iteration number. Fix: snapshot iteration into a const before the closure. One-line fix.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #485. Handles phased tool call events from ACP SDK 0.14+: translator emits summaries when rawInput arrives late, deduplication in session display/stats/search. 7 new tests, all CI green.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T18:40:27.141Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T18:51:36.061Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T21:36:33.124Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5YP6NKF3TE6KJH7XKTZMXP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T19:12:46.772Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Fixed closure capture bug in ralph event logging. The agent's update event handler persisted across iterations but captured a stale for-loop let binding. Added currentIteration outer mutable variable that gets updated each iteration. 2 static analysis regression tests. All 159 ralph tests + full suite (3227) pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ62NKTRBZZVSW0Y8DAC09YY\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-iteration-boundary-counting\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement index-based iteration boundary counting in computeIterationSummaries\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@session-log-show\",\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@plan-sequence-based-iteration-counting-for-session-anal\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #486. Implemented index-based iteration boundary counting using prompt.sent events, with legacy fallback for older sessions.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"cli\",\n      \"bug\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T20:22:21.784Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T22:31:18.626Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T23:02:12.592Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ62NKTRCQXDK9YJ6GJ9H337\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T20:22:21.784Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Rewrite computeIterationSummaries() in src/sessions/store.ts to use\\nprompt.sent event positions as iteration boundaries instead of relying\\non the data.iteration field (which suffers from a closure capture race\\nin ralph's fire-and-forget event logging).\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ62QHSE8CMYZV49CCT9QNYM\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T20:23:25.230Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"## Implementation Notes\\n\\n### Problem\\ncomputeIterationSummaries() in src/sessions/store.ts:718-802 groups events by data.iteration field. Ralph's fire-and-forget appendEvent() call at src/cli/commands/ralph.ts:1573-1579 captures the loop iteration variable by closure reference. By the time the async callback executes, iteration has advanced, so streaming events get tagged with wrong iteration numbers. Result: kspec session log show reports most iterations as \\\"4 events\\\" when they had hundreds.\\n\\nA separate task (@01KJ5WV0) fixes the capture-by-value bug in ralph.ts. This task makes the counting system resilient to producer-side data errors.\\n\\n### Approach: Index-Based Boundary Splitting\\nRalph emits awaited prompt.sent events with { phase: \\\"task-work\\\", iteration: N } at ralph.ts:1463 at the start of each iteration. Use these as authoritative iteration boundaries.\\n\\nCRITICAL: Use array indices from readEvents() output, NOT seq values. appendEvent() is explicitly not concurrency-safe (store.ts:260) — concurrent fire-and-forget calls can produce duplicate seq numbers. Array indices provide deterministic splitting immune to seq races.\\n\\n### Algorithm\\n1. Read all events via readEvents() (returns sorted array)\\n2. Find boundary events: type === \\\"prompt.sent\\\" AND data?.phase === \\\"task-work\\\" AND typeof data?.iteration === \\\"number\\\" — record their array index and iteration number\\n3. Validate: filter out non-monotonic iteration numbers, deduplicate\\n4. If no valid boundaries → legacy fallback (current data.iteration grouping, extracted into helper function)\\n5. Build index ranges: [0, boundary1.idx), [boundary1.idx, boundary2.idx), etc.\\n6. Pre-boundary events merge into first iteration\\n7. Extract tasks_started/tasks_completed per iteration (unchanged logic)\\n\\n### Files to Modify\\nsrc/sessions/store.ts:\\n- Rewrite computeIterationSummaries() (lines 718-802) with boundary algorithm\\n- Extract current logic into legacyIterationGrouping() helper for fallback\\n- Update getSessionLogDetail() (~line 820) to derive iteration_count from summaries.length instead of calling countIterations() separately\\n- Add countIterationsBoundaryAware() — lightweight boundary counter for getSessionLogSummary() (used by session log list and session log stats) to prevent iteration_count disagreements between list and show views\\n\\ntests/session-log-show.test.ts:\\n- Update existing fixtures (~line 171) to include phase: \\\"task-work\\\" field\\n- Add tests:\\n  1. Multi-iteration with prompt.sent boundaries (index-based grouping)\\n  2. Wrong data.iteration on streaming events (still grouped correctly)\\n  3. Legacy fallback — no prompt.sent events with phase field\\n  4. Malformed boundaries — prompt.sent with missing phase/iteration (graceful fallback)\\n  5. Single iteration — one boundary captures all events\\n  6. Pre-loop events — session.start before first prompt.sent merged into iteration 1\\n  7. Mixed phase prompt.sent — both task-work and reflect present, only task-work used\\n  8. Duplicate seq values — concurrent events with same seq, boundary math correct\\n\\n### Key Implementation Details\\n- SessionEvent.data is typed as unknown (types.ts:105) — treat boundary data as untrusted, validate phase and iteration fields before use\\n- readEvents() at store.ts:320-340 sorts by seq — index order follows seq order\\n- Reflect prompt.sent uses phase: \\\"reflect\\\" (ralph.ts:1648) — safely excluded\\n- Subagents and wrap-up agents don't emit prompt.sent to parent session (confirmed in src/ralph/subagent.ts:229)\\n- No changes needed to types.ts, ralph.ts, or session.ts\\n\\n### Verification\\n1. npx vitest run tests/session-log-show.test.ts\\n2. npm run dev -- session log show 01KJ4VNM — verify accurate counts across all iterations (not \\\"4 events\\\" for most)\\n3. Cross-check: session log list iteration counts match session log show\\n4. Full suite: npx vitest run\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6ABC15HHM9PSNPMETWRDFN\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T22:36:34.725Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented index-based iteration boundary counting. computeIterationSummaries() now finds prompt.sent events with phase: 'task-work' as boundaries, splits events by array index ranges. Legacy fallback preserved for sessions without boundaries. Added countIterationsBoundaryAware() for getSessionLogSummary() consistency. getSessionLogDetail() now derives iteration_count from summaries.length. 8 new test cases covering: boundary grouping, wrong data.iteration resilience, legacy fallback, pre-boundary merging, single iteration, mixed phases, malformed boundaries, duplicate seq values. All 35 session-log-show tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ65H0N4F3TK1A9EZRSZAHBT\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Design native task-limit enforcement for ralph agent iterations\",\n    \"type\": \"spike\",\n    \"description\": \"## Problem\\n\\nRalph loop agents are not stopping after completing one task per iteration. Evidence from session 01KJ5WZPNDYY68ZX143D06FXCB shows an agent submitted task @01KJ4SMA, then immediately started and completed task @01KJ5WV0 with zero ralph intervention between them. The maxTasks: 1 setting was never enforced.\\n\\nTwo root causes:\\n\\n1. **No event-to-agent tracking**: Ralph has no way to attribute a `kspec task submit` or `kspec task complete` to the currently active agent iteration. The marker file approach is passive — ralph writes it, but only when it detects a complete command in the event stream. Since the agent used `submit` (not `complete`), the marker was never written.\\n\\n2. **Submit not treated as completion**: `detectTaskCompleteCommand()` in ralph.ts (line 229) explicitly excludes `kspec task submit`. But submit means the agent's work is done — a review agent should take over. Submit should count the same as complete for task-limit purposes.\\n\\n3. **Shell script hook is fragile**: The current `ralph-task-limit-guard.sh` is a shell script that parses JSON with jq, walks directories to find project root, and reads a marker file. This should be a native kspec command (like `kspec session checkpoint` is for the Stop hook) for reliability and testability.\\n\\n## Investigation Goals\\n\\n- How can ralph reliably track which events belong to the active agent? Options: session scoping, event correlation IDs, agent turn boundaries\\n- What's the right enforcement point? PreToolUse hook blocking `task start`, or injecting a stop signal, or both?\\n- Should the hook be `kspec ralph guard` or similar native command that reads ralph state directly instead of a marker file?\\n\\n## Design Deliverables\\n\\n- Clear design for native task-limit hook (replacing ralph-task-limit-guard.sh)\\n- Updated detection logic: submit counts as completion for limit purposes\\n- Event attribution approach so ralph knows what the active agent did\\n- Spec updates if the current @ralph-task-limit spec needs changes\\n- New task(s) derived from the design for implementation work\\n\\n## Key Files\\n\\n- src/cli/commands/ralph.ts (lines 227-231 detectTaskCompleteCommand, 1520-1557 limit counting, 1314-1773 main loop)\\n- .claude/hooks/ralph-task-limit-guard.sh (current shell script hook)\\n- src/cli/commands/setup.ts (hook installation, GUARD_SCRIPTS)\\n- src/cli/commands/session.ts (session checkpoint as model for native hook)\\n- .kspec/modules/cli.yaml (@ralph-task-limit spec)\\n- templates/agents-sections/06-ralph-loop.md (agent instructions)\\n- .claude/skills/task-work/SKILL.md (agent stop instructions)\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Spike complete. Investigated session scoping approach for kspec, including:\\n- Cross-harness env var research (Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Gemini CLI)\\n- Current session/ralph/hook architecture analysis\\n- Design of session-scoped budget enforcement replacing marker files + bash hooks\\n- Dual review (internal + Codex) with all MUST-FIX findings addressed\\n\\nDeliverables:\\n- Plan @plan-session-scoping-for-kspec imported with 6 specs, 10 tasks\\n- Dependencies set between tasks\\n- Specs have traits: @trait-json-output, @trait-semantic-exit-codes, @trait-error-guidance\\n- Key design decisions: budget on local filesystem (not shadow branch), single-writer guarantee, cooperative enforcement, end-loop migrated to session state, sessions always closed\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"ralph\",\n      \"hooks\",\n      \"design\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T21:12:16.803Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-24T00:42:18.887Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T01:19:28.006Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6JZEJADFS9RJ2EVEW27WWQ\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T01:07:21.290Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"## Session Progress — Spike Investigation Complete, Plan Drafted\\n\\n### What was done\\n1. **Full investigation of session scoping approach** — explored current session infrastructure, ralph loop, hooks, task schema, and environment variable handling across 4 agent harnesses (Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Gemini CLI).\\n\\n2. **Design decisions made with user:**\\n   - Soft advisory task claiming (not hard isolation)\\n   - Budget enforcement built into kspec task start itself (no hook needed for task limiting)\\n   - Session state machine: ralph unlocks → agent starts task → agent submits → kspec auto-locks → ralph resets for next iteration\\n   - Single-writer guarantee for atomicity (ralph and agent are never concurrent)\\n   - KSPEC_SESSION_ID env var flows through agent tool calls\\n\\n3. **Plan written in kspec import format** at `/home/chapel/.claude/plans/bright-seeking-marble.md`:\\n   - 5 specs: session-creation-and-env-injection, session-scoped-task-claiming, task-budget-enforcement, native-guard-commands, ralph-session-budget-integration\\n   - 9 tasks covering schema changes, CLI commands, budget enforcement, native guards, ralph simplification, multi-harness env injection\\n   - Dry run passes clean: `kspec plan import --module cli --dry-run`\\n\\n4. **Dual review completed** — both an internal agent review and Codex review-plan found convergent issues. Reviews saved at `/tmp/codex-plan-review.md`.\\n\\n### Review findings to address before import\\nMUST-FIX:\\n- Add ACs for invalid/stale KSPEC_SESSION_ID (session not found, malformed ID)\\n- Add migration cleanup ACs (remove old hook entries from settings.json, delete old bash scripts)\\n- Add cross-file consistency ACs (task state + budget state divergence on partial failure)\\n- Fix `ac-cleanup` to be concrete and testable\\n\\nSHOULD-FIX (under discussion with user):\\n- Shadow branch contention: should budget state live in local file vs shadow branch?\\n- Submit vs complete with review subagent: should subagent inherit session ID?\\n- End-loop marker: leave as-is or migrate to session state?\\n- Wrap-up message: error message should contain wrap-up instructions\\n- Explicitly state interactive sessions have no budget\\n- Fix file reference: `tasks ready` is in tasks.ts not task.ts\\n- State explicitly that enforcement is cooperative-only\\n\\n### What's left\\n- User wants to discuss specific findings (shadow branch contention, subagent session inheritance, end-loop marker, wrap-up message) before updating the plan\\n- After discussion: update plan with fixes, re-run dry run, import\\n- Then: derive implementation tasks from the plan\\n\\n### Key files\\n- Plan: /home/chapel/.claude/plans/bright-seeking-marble.md\\n- Codex review: /tmp/codex-plan-review.md\\n- Internal review: in conversation context\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6KNM8DXMMSBTQG7R6G9KHQ\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T01:19:28.013Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Completed with --skip-review: Spike complete. Investigated session scoping approach for kspec, including:\\n- Cross-harness env var research (Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Gemini CLI)\\n- Current session/ralph/hook architecture analysis\\n- Design of session-scoped budget enforcement replacing marker files + bash hooks\\n- Dual review (internal + Codex) with all MUST-FIX findings addressed\\n\\nDeliverables:\\n- Plan @plan-session-scoping-for-kspec imported with 6 specs, 10 tasks\\n- Dependencies set between tasks\\n- Specs have traits: @trait-json-output, @trait-semantic-exit-codes, @trait-error-guidance\\n- Key design decisions: budget on local filesystem (not shadow branch), single-writer guarantee, cooperative enforcement, end-loop migrated to session state, sessions always closed\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"manual_only\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ65J2Q0SS2WGYD1P5FZ2C40\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Fix phased tool call event handling for ralph display and session stats\",\n    \"type\": \"bug\",\n    \"description\": \"## Problem\\n\\nAfter upgrading to @agentclientprotocol/sdk@0.14.x, tool call info (command names, file paths, etc.) is no longer displayed in ralph loop output. Only the tool result/output is shown.\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\nThe ACP SDK now sends tool calls in two phases:\\n1. `tool_call` event with `rawInput: {}` (empty) and `status: pending`\\n2. `tool_call_update` event moments later with populated `rawInput: { command: \\\"...\\\", description: \\\"...\\\" }`\\n\\nThe event translator in events.ts extracts the summary on the first event (gets empty string from empty rawInput), then when the second event arrives with populated input, the logic at line 648 doesn't always re-emit a tool_update with the now-available summary.\\n\\n## Affected Code (comprehensive list)\\n\\n### Core translator (primary fix)\\n- **src/ralph/events.ts lines 632-683** (`tool_call` case): Summary extraction from empty rawInput yields \\\"\\\". Need to handle phased arrival — when tool_call_update arrives with populated rawInput and existing summary was empty, emit a tool_update event with the summary.\\n- **src/ralph/events.ts line 648**: The check `if (summary && !hadSummary)` — needs to correctly detect \\\"summary was empty before, now has content\\\"\\n- **src/ralph/events.ts lines 685-738** (`tool_call_update` case): May need to also check for newly-available summary here, not just in the tool_call case\\n\\n### CLI renderer (may need adjustment)\\n- **src/ralph/cli-renderer.ts lines 175-198** (`renderToolStart`): Currently shows empty summary on first event. Should either defer display until summary available, or update display when summary arrives via tool_update\\n- **src/ralph/cli-renderer.ts lines 200-211** (`renderToolUpdate`): Should display summary when it arrives in the update phase\\n\\n### Session stats (double-counting bug)\\n- **src/sessions/store.ts lines 979-1028** (`computeToolUsageStats`): Counts BOTH phased events as separate tool calls, leading to doubled tool usage stats. Must deduplicate by toolCallId — only count unique tool calls, not phased updates\\n- **src/sessions/store.ts lines 455-484** (`countTaskCompletions`): Accesses `rawInput.command` — safe since first event has empty rawInput (won't false-match), but should be verified\\n\\n### Session display\\n- **src/cli/commands/session.ts lines 1508-1556** (`summarizeEventData`): Shows tool_call events — first phased event will show only tool name without command details. Should either skip events with empty rawInput or prefer the populated version\\n- **src/cli/commands/session.ts lines 1646-1737** (`sessionLogShowAction`): Displays events, may show tool twice (once per phase)\\n- **src/cli/commands/session.ts lines 1856-1924** (`sessionLogStatsAction`): Uses computeToolUsageStats — inherits double-counting bug\\n- **src/cli/commands/session.ts lines 1992-2027** (`sessionLogSearchAction`): Searches events, may find duplicate matches for phased events\\n\\n### Iteration summaries\\n- **src/sessions/store.ts lines 718-802** (`computeIterationSummaries`): Extracts task start/complete refs from rawInput.command at lines 780-789 — only works when rawInput populated (second event), which is correct but should be documented\\n\\n## Test Coverage Needed\\n\\n### Existing tests to update\\n- **tests/session-log-stats.test.ts lines 187-210**: Tests computeToolUsageStats with single events only — need phased event pair tests to verify no double-counting\\n- **tests/ralph.test.ts**: Tests event translation — need phased tool_call event pairs\\n\\n### New tests needed\\n- Phased tool_call → tool_call (with input) → tool_call_update (completed) flow through translator\\n- Tool usage stats with phased events (verify count = 1, not 2)\\n- CLI renderer output for phased events (summary appears on update, not on empty start)\\n- Session log show/search with phased events (no duplicates)\\n\\n## Fix Approach\\n\\n1. **Translator (events.ts)**: When a tool_call or tool_call_update arrives with populated rawInput for a toolCallId whose existing summary is empty, extract the new summary and emit a tool_update event\\n2. **Stats (store.ts)**: Deduplicate tool_call events by toolCallId — track seen IDs and only count first occurrence\\n3. **Session display (session.ts)**: Filter or merge phased events so display shows one entry per tool call with full details\\n4. **Tests**: Add phased event fixtures and assertions across all affected test files\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"PR #485 merged by @chapel. Fix handles phased tool call events from ACP SDK 0.14+: translator extracts summary from tool_call_update, stats deduplicate by toolCallId, session display filters phased duplicates.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"ralph\",\n      \"events\",\n      \"acp\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T21:12:51.679Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T21:18:50.746Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T21:37:01.844Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ65Y495V3GKE9TKZ3DWCVHD\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T21:19:26.501Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Starting work. Three areas to fix: (1) translator in events.ts - handle summary in tool_call_update with rawInput, (2) store.ts computeToolUsageStats - dedup by toolCallId, (3) session display/search - dedup phased events at read time.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ66DC1P1P3AZK08GRXNZDER\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T21:27:45.974Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Fixed three issues with ACP SDK 0.14+ phased tool call events: (1) translator now extracts summary from tool_call_update with newly-populated rawInput, (2) computeToolUsageStats deduplicates by toolCallId, (3) session show/search filter phased duplicates. 7 new tests, all 3234 tests pass. Local review: PASS, no MUST-FIX items.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6B1E8F4QX8JMBMJ9SC8MCA\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-session-show-trait-ac-coverage\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Add missing trait AC test annotations for session-log-show\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Audit tests/session-log-show.test.ts for missing trait AC annotations. Codex review of PR #486 found gaps: @trait-json-output ac-2, ac-4, ac-6 and @trait-semantic-exit-codes ac-2, ac-3, ac-5, ac-6, ac-7, ac-8. Some may be N/A for this command (e.g. user cancellation, batch partial failures) — mark those as not applicable in the spec or add tests where applicable.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@session-log-show\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #497. Added 10 trait AC tests for session-log-show: @trait-json-output (ac-2, ac-4, ac-6) and @trait-semantic-exit-codes (ac-2, ac-6, ac-8). Documented 3 N/A cases (ac-3, ac-5, ac-7). All review findings addressed in fix commit.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"cli\",\n      \"testing\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T22:48:37.903Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-24T05:06:52.800Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T05:25:17.958Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ719YVQ849FGY56NAV6NEF7\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T05:17:45.719Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Added 10 new trait AC tests for session-log-show: @trait-json-output (ac-2, ac-4, ac-6) and @trait-semantic-exit-codes (ac-2, ac-6, ac-8). Documented N/A cases for ac-3/ac-5/ac-7. Codex review raised 3 findings (exit code assertions too weak, trait spec mismatch, test naming) — all addressed in fix commit. PR #497.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6CJC3TDT5PG0E6YV184MVJ\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-cleanup-obsolete-skills\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Clean up obsolete project skills superseded by core skills\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"After the skill porting effort, .claude/skills/ still contains old versions of skills that were rewritten as core skills in templates/skills/. These should be removed.\\n\\nDuplicates (exist in both .claude/skills/ and templates/skills/):\\n- create-workflow — ported to kspec:create-workflow\\n- reflect — ported to kspec:reflect\\n- task-work — ported to kspec:task-work\\n\\nRenamed/replaced (old name in .claude/skills/, new core version in templates/skills/):\\n- meta → kspec:observations\\n- spec → kspec:writing-specs\\n- spec-plan → kspec:plan\\n\\nAction: Remove the 6 obsolete skills from .claude/skills/. Verify no references remain in settings.json, CLAUDE.md, or other config. Confirm core versions fully cover functionality before deleting.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Removed 6 obsolete project skills (create-workflow, reflect, task-work, meta, spec, spec-plan) from .claude/skills/. All content verified covered by core skills. Committed in 91e26c52.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"cli\",\n      \"skills\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T23:15:21.338Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-23T23:38:36.688Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T23:45:15.063Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6DYTXTSDVD3X12DWH2NZ76\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T23:39:38.299Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Completed full comparison of all 6 old skills vs core replacements. All content is covered by core skills. The one notable difference is meta→observations (old covered focus/threads/questions/observations, core covers observations only — but focus/threads/questions are lightweight CLI features in kspec help meta, not needing a dedicated skill). Ready to delete the 6 old skills and clean up references, pending user confirmation.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6E8A32DZTXNAJNTKNFX1V6\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T23:44:48.738Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Removed 6 obsolete skills from .claude/skills/: create-workflow, reflect, task-work, meta, spec, spec-plan. Verified no stale references in settings.json or CLAUDE.md. Test files reference .claude/skills/task-work as a core skill install target (correct behavior, not old skill). 9 project-specific skills remain: audit, codex, e2e, eval-agents, local-review, pr, pr-review, release, svelte-5.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6E93SRXZ9AJAR53A15Q7A5\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T23:45:15.064Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Completed with --force from in_progress state. Reason: Removed 6 obsolete project skills (create-workflow, reflect, task-work, meta, spec, spec-plan) from .claude/skills/. All content verified covered by core skills. Committed in 91e26c52.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6KKPZGG5ZWXJHEC69CYPZK\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"extend-session-schema-with-task-budget\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Extend session schema with task budget\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@session-creation-and-env-injection\",\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@plan-session-scoping-for-kspec\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #498. Added TaskBudgetSchema and 5 budget CRUD functions (createBudget, getBudget, checkBudget, incrementBudget, resetBudget) to sessions module. Budget stored at .kspec/sessions/{id}/budget.json (local FS, not shadow branch) with atomic writes. getBudget fails closed on corruption (only ENOENT returns null). 32 tests. Codex review finding addressed.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"schema\",\n      \"sessions\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T01:18:25.264Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-24T05:25:39.126Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T05:47:29.345Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6KKPZGVX8AHJHP2CHZPQTP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T01:18:25.264Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Add TaskBudgetSchema to src/sessions/types.ts. Budget stored in local filesystem\\nat .kspec/sessions/{id}/budget.json (NOT shadow branch). Add incrementBudget(),\\nresetBudget(), checkBudget() functions to src/sessions/store.ts. Atomic writes\\nvia write-to-temp-then-rename pattern. Single-writer guarantee documented.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ72KGJ0MCQ7V3V7Q3YJ9RRH\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T05:40:27.328Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Added TaskBudgetSchema (max_per_cycle: positive int, started_this_cycle: nonneg int) to sessions/types.ts. Added 5 budget CRUD functions (createBudget, getBudget, checkBudget, incrementBudget, resetBudget) to sessions/store.ts with atomic write-to-temp-then-rename. Budget stored at .kspec/sessions/{id}/budget.json (local filesystem, not shadow branch). Codex review caught MUST-FIX: getBudget was failing open on corrupt files — fixed to only return null for ENOENT, throwing on parse/validation errors. 32 tests. PR #498.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6KKQA3E86SF0YNDS2R705X\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"add-session-id-to-task-schema\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Add session_id to task schema\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@session-scoped-task-claiming\",\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@plan-session-scoping-for-kspec\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #499. Added session_id field to TaskSchema/TaskInputSchema, session stamping on task start, warning for cross-session claiming, session indicator in output, and session_id clearing on status transitions. All 6 ACs covered with 13 integration tests. CI green.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"schema\",\n      \"tasks\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T01:18:25.603Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-24T05:48:02.012Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T06:16:49.002Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6KKQA3JTQGS8FWWKWTBYVK\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T01:18:25.603Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Add optional session_id field to TaskSchema and TaskInputSchema in\\nsrc/schema/task.ts. Single line addition: session_id: z.string().optional().\\nClear session_id on status transitions back to pending or needs_work.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ73HYFTGFD97X3VSDSY5VGC\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T05:57:04.635Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented session-scoped task claiming. Added session_id field to TaskSchema and TaskInputSchema (optional, nullable, backward compatible). Task start reads KSPEC_SESSION_ID env var and stamps task. Warns when task is claimed by another session. Session indicator shown in task list and details. session_id cleared on transitions to pending (unblock, reset) and needs_work. 13 integration tests covering all 6 ACs.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ74P33B587CZQM3FNS7F9EP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T06:16:49.003Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Completed with --skip-review: Merged in PR #499. Added session_id field to TaskSchema/TaskInputSchema, session stamping on task start, warning for cross-session claiming, session indicator in output, and session_id clearing on status transitions. All 6 ACs covered with 13 integration tests. CI green.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6KKQM5WQKJKP7B1BAY0RB2\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"implement-session-create-command\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement session create command\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@session-creation-and-env-injection\",\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@plan-session-scoping-for-kspec\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #500. Implements session create CLI command and createSessionWithBudget() library function with env injection for Claude Code, Codex CLI, and fallback. All 8 spec ACs covered, trait ACs tested. Fix commit addressed all 7 review findings.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@extend-session-schema-with-task-budget\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"cli\",\n      \"sessions\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T01:18:25.925Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-24T06:27:32.561Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T06:54:59.114Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6KKQM59XEDXGADGFGMCB65\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T01:18:25.925Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Add session create subcommand to src/cli/commands/session.ts. Creates session\\nwith optional --budget flag. Returns session ID on stdout. Also exposes\\ncreateSessionWithBudget() library function for ralph to call directly.\\nInclude validation for invalid/stale KSPEC_SESSION_ID with clear error messages.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ759CHH0PBSVV54RMMW1DG7\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T06:27:21.266Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented session create command and library function. Added createSessionWithBudget() to store.ts, validateSessionId() for invalid session handling, env injection functions (Claude Code via CLAUDE_ENV_FILE or .claude/settings.json, Codex via config.json shell_environment_policy.set, fallback export command). CLI command registered as 'session create' with --agent-type, --budget, --inject, --task-id flags. 29 tests covering all 8 own ACs and key trait ACs (json-output, semantic-exit-codes, error-guidance).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6KKQZR2FPQRPWJ74C4AKJP\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"add-budget-enforcement-to-task-start\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Add budget enforcement to task start\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@task-budget-enforcement\",\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@plan-session-scoping-for-kspec\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged PR #501. Budget enforcement added to task start — checks session budget before allowing start, increments counter after successful transition, skips for resume/no-session/no-budget cases. 17 tests covering all 7 own ACs and 8 trait ACs (with N/A documented for non-applicable ones). All review threads resolved, CI green.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@extend-session-schema-with-task-budget\",\n      \"@add-session-id-to-task-schema\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"cli\",\n      \"tasks\",\n      \"enforcement\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T01:18:26.296Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-24T07:14:25.492Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T07:27:52.352Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ6KKQZRCB3WS60T0K0JWYGM\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T01:18:26.296Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Modify task start handler (~line 1068 in src/cli/commands/task.ts) to check\\nsession budget before proceeding. Read KSPEC_SESSION_ID from process.env, read\\nbudget.json, check started_this_cycle vs max_per_cycle. On success increment\\ncounter. Error message must include budget counts AND wrap-up instructions\\n(replaces both hook block message and ralph prompt injection). Skip increment\\nwhen task is already in_progress (resume case). Also stamp session_id on task.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ77AZ5MTXNPH6R32MSKNNK5\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T07:03:10.260Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented budget enforcement in task start handler. Added checkBudget() call before task transition (blocks with exit 4 + error guidance when exhausted). Added incrementBudget() call after successful start (skipped for resume case since already in_progress returns early). 17 integration tests covering all 7 own ACs and 6 trait ACs (semantic-exit-codes ac-1/ac-4, error-guidance ac-1/ac-2/ac-5/ac-6).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ77NW4RHCFPP4MRF0XVTBXN\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T07:09:07.608Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: Review passed — code and tests are clean, all ACs covered, no MUST-FIX or SHOULD-FIX items. However, changes are uncommitted and no PR exists. Worker needs to: (1) commit changes, (2) push branch, (3) create PR, (4) resubmit for merge.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJ77X862H1V2KTHEQ8VSYSW6\",\n        